{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition","id":1528721,"title":"Ten Tips to running the Cult of Fenris in Werewolf Fifth Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-17T10:54:19-08:00","id":1528721,"title":"Ten Tips to running the Cult of Fenris in Werewolf Fifth Edition","content":"<br /> <br /> <img width=\"750\" height=\"938\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhz-KuPlWoWSvpj-kLy2l2TiQrVo9rg_CdLBchFtRPYqbqQyRRN0QithD-y-kHFN-OyDzlNhI99lgNAc685NxfSOtMzKNHH75QA9G2X8TkdhKMS05FBZ1gX6uTkeQj_iwyPGfD5CBzTr_PI7qoN4cn4VGMaEdYyQkSNESOV60wf0y7TulX9LMenVN6OMf-2/s1280/RGS_Tablet_WerewolfCRB_1280pxls__29984.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhz-KuPlWoWSvpj-kLy2l2TiQrVo9rg_CdLBchFtRPYqbqQyRRN0QithD-y-kHFN-OyDzlNhI99lgNAc685NxfSOtMzKNHH75QA9G2X8TkdhKMS05FBZ1gX6uTkeQj_iwyPGfD5CBzTr_PI7qoN4cn4VGMaEdYyQkSNESOV60wf0y7TulX9LMenVN6OMf-2/s1280/RGS_Tablet_WerewolfCRB_1280pxls__29984.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhz-KuPlWoWSvpj-kLy2l2TiQrVo9rg_CdLBchFtRPYqbqQyRRN0QithD-y-kHFN-OyDzlNhI99lgNAc685NxfSOtMzKNHH75QA9G2X8TkdhKMS05FBZ1gX6uTkeQj_iwyPGfD5CBzTr_PI7qoN4cn4VGMaEdYyQkSNESOV60wf0y7TulX9LMenVN6OMf-2/s1280/RGS_Tablet_WerewolfCRB_1280pxls__29984.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2024/01/ten-tips-to-running-cult-of-fenris-in.html\" target=\"_blank\">Link: https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2024/01/ten-tips-to-running-cult-of-fenris-in.html</a></span><br /> <br /> One of the most controversial decisions of Werewolf: The Apocalypse Fifth Edition was the fall of the Get of Fenris to hauglosk and becoming the Cult of Fenris. In simple terms, this means they went from being playable PC faction to being a non-player antagonist faction. This was upsetting to many people due to the fact that they were a very popular tribe and &quot;Viking werewolves&quot; was never going to not be a common choice of PC.<br /> <br /> In <i>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</i> 5th Edition, the Get of Fenris attend a moot with the rest of the Garou Nation and state that the only way to stop the Apocalypse is for the entire Garou Nation to launch a Ragnarok-esque charge against the Wyrm's home fortress. Remembering the fate of the White Howlers, most Garou refuse and the Get of Fenris withdraw from the Garou Nation while swearing eternal enimity against their former siblings. When next encountered, they are the Cult of Fenris and engaging in horrific atrocities out of a misguided belief they are Gaia's last chance.<br /> <br /> The reasoning for this has been widely discussed and it has supporters as well as detractors over it. However, this isn't about any of that. Instead, this is about offering suggestions for those Storytellers who are intrigued by the possibilities inherent to another tribe of the Garou falling to the Wyrm (or Hauglosk in this case). It is there offer tips for making it a source of interesting stories as well as roleplaying plus potentially the center of Chronicles. It is not an attempt to persuade you whether or not the action was justified or fits with lore but merely offer perspective on a way to do it in the best way possible for Storytellers as well as players' enjoyment.<br /> <br /> I hope both will find this useful.<br /> <br /> <b>1. Make sure longtime players are comfortable with it</b><br /> <br /> The first thing to understand is whether or not your players are interested in making the transition to W5 at all as well as incorporating the Cult of Fenris' rebirth from the Get of Fenris. Some players may have no interest in the topic and would prefer to stick to a more metaplot agnostic or previous edition version of the game. This is fine and shouldn't be forced. While there is plenty of potential for this transition, ultimately what serves the enjoyment of the people at the table needs to be considered first.<br /> <br /> <b>2. Make it an event</b><br /> <br /> There's never a more dramatic period during a coup than when it's actually occurring. This is probably the case during the fall of the Get of Fenris. Imagine you your player characters are attending the faithful moot when the Get of Fenris make their insane ultimatum. The player characters may react with the belief that they have a point, they are being stupidly rash, or are outright treasonous.<br /> <br /> This offers the player characters a chance to debate the issue and possibly win some Get packs over to their side or other Garou that agree with them. You can then reveal the Get are already doomed with the slow revelation that they've stacked the deck ahead of time by eliminating those leaders who weren't onboard with their treason. You can end up going Order 66 on the Get loyalists and reveal their treachery was in the works for some time.<br /> <br /> Much like the Convention of Thorns in Vampire: The Masquerade, the Grand Moot of Fenris (or whatever you want to call it) can be an opportunity for the player characters to meet with famous NPCs as well as have a direct effect on how things shake down. Maybe they'll prevent the assassination of Albretch or the Margrave. Maybe they'll be the ones to discover that attempts to save the Get are doomed because it is Wolf itself who has been corrupted. Maybe they will lead the Loyalist Get to break ties even if it means severing their bonds to their fellows.<br /> <br /> It might be best to even start the game as Get characters.<br /> <br /> <b>3. Don't simplify it</b><br /> <br /> The corebook takes an almost comically simplistic interpretation of the Cult of Fenris. There's a lot more tragedy in the view that the Get of Fenris had a point but have since gone completely off the rails in their pursuit of it. Gaia is dying and they need to do something now to save the Earth. It may be stupid to believe you can defeat the Wyrm in Malpheas or triumph where the White Howlers failed but the call to action should not be dismissed out of hand. The player characters should now friends, loved ones, mentors, and others who have gone over to the other side even if they disagree with the cruelty. Extreme times calling for extreme measures is a seductive call for many, particularly the Garou who were aware the Earth was dying before most humans.<br /> <br /> It is fine that the Cult of Fenris are awful. That they represent the worst of Garou ideology, violence, and disdain for humans as well as other shapechangers. But there should be a method to their madness that allows Garou to know how they got from Point A to Point Z even if Z isn't helping.<br /> <br /> <b>4. Hauglosk is a symptom not a cause</b><br /> <br /> Hauglosk is a state of fanaticism and zealotry so extreme that Garou who fall to it are effectively lost. Consumed by the Dark SIde of the Force or One Ring of Power if you will. It is easy, even in-universe, for the Garou to dismiss the Cult of Fenris as having fallen to this state and being unable to saved. However, a more interesting take on this subject is that is the result of their beliefs and behaviors rather than simply the means that all of the Cutl have gone nuts. &quot;Redeeming&quot; a Cult of Fenris member, either a cub or former friend, shouldn't have Mechanics but be the result of a Session of players doing their best to reach them. Getting past the rage and sense of fear that they have failed Gaia while offering hope there is another way.<br /> <br /> <b>5. Define the spiritual nature of the crisis</b><br /> <br /> Related to the above Hauglosk entry, addressing how the Cult of Fenris have affected the Spirit World of the Garou is certainly worth a Storyteller's time. The obvious question is whether or not Wolf has been corrupted by Hauglosk or fallen to the Wyrm itself. As the totem animal of the Garou as a whole, are they all being affected or it limited to the Cult? Is it possible to heal Wolf or replace it with one of its cubs as Totem of the Get/Cult? Must it be slain? Is it even Wolf at all or is it being impersonated by the Beast of War?<br /> <br /> What affects has the tribe's fall had on their fetishes, caerns, compacts, and other spiritual relations? In previous editions, the Garou might have taken a lengthy journey into the Umbra for these answers but now might have to seek powerful new magic to survive anything longer than a short journey. Perhaps Hauglosk is a new condition and less of an innate evil fo the Garou than a sign of Wolf's own corruption spreading to their children.<br /> <br /> <b>6. The Cult's evils as Garou Evils not Human Evils</b><br /> <br /> The corebook heavily implies that the Cult of Fenris has dealings with white supremacist ideology and past groups that were wiped out by the Get of Fenris from within their ranks. In my opinion, and fully aware this going against the &quot;killing Nazis is fun&quot;, I believe STs should ignore this element. There's plenty of villainous motivations with the dying of Gaia, Garou supremacy, denial of the failure of violence as a means to save Gaia, and so on. They don't need to be racists against different kinds of humans to make them even more hateable. It's not even just in poor taste but doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> <b>7. Muddy the Cult's membership a bit</b><br /> <br /> One of the loresheets in the corebook is Renunciate of Fenris (page 298), which in its simplest terms means the player character used to be a Get of Fenris but had to join another tribe because his own went mad with Hauglosk. You can't continue to be a Get of Fenris if Wolf (Fenris) is all on Team Fanatic. The numbers aren't clear about how many of the Get who stayed behind are but you could easily go with a tenth or even up to a third without violating the spirit of things. It's possible to even have these ex-Get hoping to find a new Totem for their ex-tribemates or the PCs to want to help them. Perhaps, at the height of a campaign, the Children of Garm may emerge from Wolf's brother or the new Winter's Teeth.<br /> <br /> Equally as important is to make the Cult of Fenris not necessarily all ex-Get. Surely there are Red Talons, Gatestalkers, Silver Fangs, Shadow Lords, and others who found succor in a violent but heroic death for Gaia. If but a small number of every tribe defected to the Cult of Fenris, you may explain why the Get fell but the Cult is too powerful for the Garou as a whole to face. A bit like the antitribu of the Sabbat but, presumably, lacking their former spiritual patronage.<br /> <br /> <b>8. Using the Get as Dark Mirrors</b><br /> <br /> On a fundamental level, the Cult of Fenris is making things worse not better because they're fighting their fellow Garou instead of the Wyrm as much as anything ese. However, you can use the Cult of Fenris as a way to show exactly where the Garou erred. For example, a Cult of Fenris pack may massacre a megamart full of patrons and the State Governor may declare a national order to kill all wild wolves in the state after claiming there was an outbreak of rabies. The Cult of Fenris may start a war with the local Leeches or shapechangers because even if they're trying to heal the land, this is doing SOMETHING. There is a seductive appeal in lashing out and stupidly rushing forward that young Garou (and even many old ones) may like.<br /> <br /> <b>9. The Cult of Fenris as wildcards</b><br /> <br /> If you remove the white supremacy angle and dial down the attempts by the corebook to let us REALLY KNOW the Cult are the bad guys (I think most of us can figure that out for ourselves), the Cult of Fenris becomes an interesting thing to throw into encounters that might otherwise be straightforward. The PCs may want to stop a human trafficking ring of corporate bigwigs wanting to kidnap poor migrants to experiment on. The Cult of Fenris may show up to try to slaughter everyone, Human victims included. Maybe the PCs want to take down a chemical plant illegally poisoning a town and the Cult offers to help (offering a temporary truce) but it will make things far wilder as well as more explosive. What if the Cult and PCs both find a Lost Kin girl but the Cult offers to just let them both explain their sides so she can choose for herself?<br /> <br /> <b>10. Remember this is a tragedy</b><br /> <br /> The most important thing to remember when using the Cult of Fenris is to not dismiss their tragedy or fall. They were formerly warriors of Gaia and still consider themselves to be so. In living memory, they were the kind of people that would fight by our heroes' side and probably did. However, now they are consumed by hatred and easy answers. Their solution of simply trying what hasn't worked in the past and making it ten times more violent has no chance of working but seems better than just wringing ones claws. Now the Get kill as many Garou as the Black Spiral Dancers used to and weaken the Garou Nation's already slim chance of saving the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-17-2024, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T11:20:23-08:00","id":1528722,"title":"","content":"Few nitpicks; CoF did not fall to the Wyrm. They fell into Hauglosk and Hauglosk isn't of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Second, garou call humans humans, calling humans homids is a 1st ed thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T11:30:17-08:00","id":1528724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528722#post1528722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Few nitpicks; CoF did not fall to the Wyrm. They fell into Hauglosk and Hauglosk isn't of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Second, garou call humans humans, calling humans homids is a 1st ed thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the correction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-17-2024, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T12:57:59-08:00","id":1528737,"title":"","content":"There's Clans creeping in where you're discussing Tribes. The authors and the game stresses that this game was never the game we used to play. Unlike V5 that is a continuation of the older stories to greater or lesser extend, there is no continuation from a former plot point here, just a world that was always different from the one that used to be.<br /> <br /> Jonas Albrecht and Yuri Konietzko never existed in the world of W5. The tribes were always as they are now. The diagetic world is defined in the book and everything that came before is irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Also on your point 6) The authors themselves seem to be keen on including the themes of interlinking human racism and human fascist groups and ideals into the Cult, so your ideas don't really match with what they are presenting us in the adventures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T13:11:14-08:00","id":1528738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528737#post1528737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's Clans creeping in where you're discussing Tribes. The authors and the game stresses that this game was never the game we used to play. Unlike V5 that is a continuation of the older stories to greater or lesser extend, there is no continuation from a former plot point here, just a world that was always different from the one that used to be.<br /> <br /> Jonas Albrecht and Yuri Konietzko never existed in the world of W5. The tribes were always as they are now. The diagetic world is defined in the book and everything that came before is irrelevant..</div> </div> </div> </div>Albrecht is mentioned on page 190 in the Silver Crown entry.<br /> <br /> As a symbol of its grandeur, the Silver Fangs<br /> tribe exalts the Silver Crown, a legendary artifact<br /> belonging to the Albrecht lineage of Silver Fang<br /> werewolves. With the disappearance of the last<br /> proclaimed king of the tribe, however, two great<br /> icons of tribal esteem have been lost, which many<br /> Garou interpret as an omen about the fate of the<br /> Silver Fangs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also on your point 6) The authors themselves seem to be keen on including the themes of interlinking human racism and human fascist groups and ideals into the Cult, so your ideas don't really match with what they are presenting us in the adventures\u200b </div> </div> </div>Serious question: is it not clear that 6) is saying to go against the interpretation presented by the books?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-17-2024, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T13:14:01-08:00","id":1528739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528738#post1528738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Albrecht is mentioned on page 190 in the Silver Crown entry.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no &quot;Albrecht line&quot; in Legacy material. He is part of the Morningkill line.The authors explicitly said that this world was always like this and there was never any point of connection or flow from the old to the new.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T13:15:32-08:00","id":1528740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528739#post1528739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is no &quot;Albrecht line&quot; in Legacy material. He is part of the Morningkill line.The authors explicitly said that this world was always like this and there was never any point of connection or flow from the old to the new.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you don't think the last great self-proclaimed king is a reference to Albrecht?<br /> <br /> Also, to be pedantic, he was House Wyrmfoe not Morningkill.<br /> <br /> Morningkill and Albrecht were both surnames.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-17-2024, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T13:22:58-08:00","id":1528741,"title":"","content":"This won't be coherent with how the Cult is written about in the official material. I've only run W5 once using the scenario from the corebook and I don't really plan to run it again but if I were... Here are the key-points I would use (while ignoring the written official material):<ul><li><b>The Cult of Fenris is an ideology, not a Tribe:</b> The question at the heart of the Cult of Fenris is what it means to be a Garou in the Age of Apocalypse. In fact, the Cult-members believe they have more of a reason to call themselves Garou than the non-Cult-Garou do.</li> <li><b>The Cult of Fenris thinks the Garou Nation's biggest issue was that it wasn't led by the &quot;strong&quot;:</b> The definition of what &quot;strong&quot; means heavily centers around beliefs you would normally call authoritarianism and fundamentalism. Conveniently the leaders of the Cult always happen to meet the criteria of &quot;strong&quot; while non-Cult Garou-leaders always fail them. The main-thing is that the Cult exists in opposition to the Garou-Nation of the past. What the Cult claims to aim for is a &quot;revived Garou-Nation - but better&quot;. What it does instead is act like a cult that is evangelizing and wants to expand.</li> <li><b>The Garou traditions are great when they agree with what the Cult wants to do and the reason the Garou-Nation fell when they don't:</b> There's no coherent reasoning as to why the Cult-members think they're better at being Garou than non-Cult-Garou. Hypocrisy is unavoidable and consistently ignored by the Cult-members. In the same way, the ethics and norms of the Garou-Nation are selectively invoked and ignored when the Cult interacts with other Garou. In the end, the only rule the Cult believes in is &quot;might makes right&quot; but occasionally at Moots some Cult-members will go to great lengths (with arguments that range from provocative calls for more aggression to convoluted diatribes that miss the forest for the trees complaining about things like &quot;The Garou have gone soft.&quot;) to make a case for why the Cult of Fenris hasn't done anything wrong.</li> <li><b>The Cult Of Fenris is a Cult:</b> Another way the Cult of Fenris operates is by propagating QAnon-style conspiracy-theories about how the world operates but also how things can be turned around for the better. Maybe it's a spirit or an authoritarian leader but the conspiratorial worldview is based on lies with only a single person or a couple of people knowing that it's all lies while the majority are true believers. It isn't a Cult just because of what they oppose but also because they believe that they know how to fix the world. But it's just a belief.</li> </ul><br /> Of course, that stuff makes it more of an antagonist-faction but that only addresses the fictional side of things. As for the ST-player-side, this is how I would address that (and once again this ignores what the W5 corebook proposes):<ul><li><b>Hauglosk is about the player:</b> Chronicle Tenets are chosen by the players and they are linked intimately to Hauglosk, so Chronicle Tenets shouldn't be treated as mere indicators of a campaign's tone and vibe. Instead, it should be important to turn these Tenets into specific things the players believe Garou should do.</li> <li><b>Members of the Cult of Fenris are there to show why Garou are bad - and why they need to be better:</b> The same way the Sabbat in VtM can serve as a reminder of what it means to not follow Humanity as a vampire, the Cult is a way to illustrate how destructive Garou can be. The behavior of Cult-members demonstrates what the PCs shouldn't be like or do. That way you present the good values of the Garou by showing Cult-of-Fenris-members abusing these values or ignoring them.</li> <li><b>Members of the Cult of Fenris are there to show why Garou are bad - and why they can be better:</b> It's a cult. You can leave it - but making that happen is <i>hard</i>. But the same way the Cult is an expression of the Garou-Nation's descent, there's hope for a revived Garou-Nation that goes in the opposite direction. It's a struggle and that's where the PCs come in. The Cult is one direction for the Garou to choose - but it isn't the only one. The players should be critical of what Garou are like and believe in but they should also see the good in what Garou can do. (Of course, this runs into the obvious issue with the W5 corebook that it offers 99% pessimism when it comes to Garou and so it's hard to figure out whether W5 officially even believes that Garou can do good)</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T13:27:28-08:00","id":1528744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528740#post1528740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you don't think the last great self-proclaimed king is a reference to Albrecht?<br /> <br /> Also, to be pedantic, he was House Wyrmfoe not Morningkill.<br /> <br /> Morningkill and Albrecht were both surnames.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I hate how you have this lovely ability to quote things without context or reading what the author is talking about. W5 introduces the concept of Silver Fang lineages, and claims that the Albrecht lineage was the last known bearer of the Silver Crown. Considering how the Silver Fangs are explained, by lineage they mean family lineage.<br /> <br /> There is no Albrech lineage in Legacy. He is a part of the Morningkill lineage - a family line leading through a whole series of legendary heroes that had the name Morningkill, and he would have also carried it were it not for the fact that his grandfather was a spiteful bastard that treated him like shit and exiled him. The Morningkill lineage belongs to House Wyrmfoe. Silver Fang Houses do not exist in W5.<br /> <br /> As for the Silver Crown itself... it's not hereditary. It's a legendary artifact that needs to be quested for and that Albrecht brought back with the blessing of the Falcon itself. This whole reference is just that, a reference to a marketable name. And it's an ass of a reference as it completley misunderstands who Albrecht was and what he did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T13:31:37-08:00","id":1528745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528744#post1528744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, I hate how you have this lovely ability to quote things without context or reading what the author is talking about. W5 introduces the concept of Silver Fang lineages, and claims that the Albrecht lineage was the last known bearer of the Silver Crown. Considering how the Silver Fangs are explained, by lineage they mean family lineage.<br /> <br /> There is no Albrech lineage in Legacy. He is a part of the Morningkill lineage - a family line leading through a whole series of legendary heroes that had the name Morningkill, and he would have also carried it were it not for the fact that his grandfather was a spiteful bastard that treated him like shit and exiled him. The Morningkill lineage belongs to House Wyrmfoe. Silver Fang Houses do not exist in W5.<br /> <br /> As for the Silver Crown itself... it's not hereditary. It's a legendary artifact that needs to be quested for and that Albrecht brought back with the blessing of the Falcon itself. This whole reference is just that, a reference to a marketable name. And it's an ass of a reference as it completley misunderstands who Albrecht was and what he did.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, I think where we may be having an issue is that I've read THE SILVER CROWN (novel) and the Albrechts flat out are in fact Jonas' family.<br /> <br /> Kin families had the king's ear and were making fu ll use<br /> of the opportunity. Apparently there was a dispute between<br /> the Rothchilds and the Albrechts, for Darren Rothchild and<br /> Warren Albrecht both argued before the king. Page 6.<br /> <br /> We meet Jonas' human father and he is, in fact, named Albrecht.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T13:36:05-08:00","id":1528746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528745#post1528745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I admit, I think where we may be having an issue is that I've read THE SILVER CROWN (novel) and the Albrechts flat out are in fact Jonas' family.<br /> <br /> Kin families had the king's ear and were making fu ll use<br /> of the opportunity. Apparently there was a dispute between<br /> the Rothchilds and the Albrechts, for Darren Rothchild and<br /> Warren Albrecht both argued before the king. Page 6.<br /> <br /> We meet Jonas' human father and he is, in fact, named Albrecht.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the name he's born under. If he had been accepted as a true descendant of Jacob he would also be bearing the name of Morningkill. Note how his name is rather nonstandard for a Werewolf, with just a name-surname and a lack of any deed name. Does Morningkill sound like a surname to you? Or more like a deed name? Maybe one handed from family member to family member?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T13:57:50-08:00","id":1528747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528738#post1528738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Serious question: is it not clear that 6) is saying to go against the interpretation presented by the books?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I honestly understood that as &quot;Killing Nazis is fun, therefore Cult as Nazis are great as enemies!&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T14:02:31-08:00","id":1528748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528747#post1528747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I honestly understood that as &quot;Killing Nazis is fun, therefore Cult as Nazis are great as enemies!&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Weird because what I wanted to say was, &quot;The Cult being Nazis is fucking stupid and you shouldn't do it.&quot;<br /> <br /> The core book thinks they should be Nazis and I'm like, &quot;No.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.am