call themselves the Warriors of Fenris, or the Followers of Fenris or something along those lines, whereas other werewolves would call them the Cult of Fenris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T19:53:52-08:00","id":1528772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528771#post1528771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question I had is, does the Cult of Fenris call itself the &quot;Cult&quot; of Fenris? In the modern era, cult has a pretty negative connotation and few modern day cults actually label themselves as cults. I'd think that they would call themselves the Warriors of Fenris, or the Followers of Fenris or something along those lines, whereas other werewolves would call them the Cult of Fenris.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it sounds better in Crinos form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T22:28:34-08:00","id":1528778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528772#post1528772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe it sounds better in Crinos form.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might in Legacy, but Crinos speaks even less in its present Great Value Gauru form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T01:04:46-08:00","id":1528783,"title":"","content":"For me, the biggest question is what do the CoF DO that makes them the bad guys?<br /> <br /> This is how I see it; Instead of Sons of Heimindal, these guys are an extreme version of the Hand of Tyr. They dedicate themselves totally to the task with zero distractions. They are also a death cult and so they refuse to take mates and basically focus solely on zerg rushing the enemy out in the open.<br /> <br /> This way, they do not copy the BSDs and still have that Gaian angle. But they lack touchstones and refuse any sort of destressing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T05:20:18-08:00","id":1528786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528783#post1528783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, the biggest question is what do the CoF DO that makes them the bad guys?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're killing their fellow Garou for being insufficiently ideologically pure.<br /> <br /> I mean, all of the Cult of Fenris examples are also frothing insane baddies too. The biggest issue of the Cult of Fenris is that they are not so much that different from other Gaian Garou but they have absolutely no ability to self-reflect, interpret the situation with nuance, or react with anything other than punishing violence as well as ideological extremism.<br /> <br /> They're not just baddies but STUPID baddies who will kill you for disagreeing with them.<br /> <br /> &quot;But I agree All Cops are Bastards.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;But you don't agree they should all be eaten!&quot;<br /> <br /> Everyone has dealt with them on the internet but now with claws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-18-2024, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T06:41:26-08:00","id":1528794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528786#post1528786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're killing their fellow Garou for being insufficiently ideologically pure.<br /> <br /> I mean, all of the Cult of Fenris examples are also frothing insane baddies too. The biggest issue of the Cult of Fenris is that they are not so much that different from other Gaian Garou but they have absolutely no ability to self-reflect, interpret the situation with nuance, or react with anything other than punishing violence as well as ideological extremism.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't all they do, though. I wanted to focus on things they do outside fighting other garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T12:03:09-08:00","id":1528822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528786#post1528786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're killing their fellow Garou for being insufficiently ideologically pure.<br /> <br /> I mean, all of the Cult of Fenris examples are also frothing insane baddies too. The biggest issue of the Cult of Fenris is that they are not so much that different from other Gaian Garou but they have absolutely no ability to self-reflect, interpret the situation with nuance, or react with anything other than punishing violence as well as ideological extremism.<br /> <br /> They're not just baddies but STUPID baddies who will kill you for disagreeing with them.<br /> <br /> &quot;But I agree All Cops are Bastards.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;But you don't agree they should all be eaten!&quot;<br /> <br /> Everyone has dealt with them on the internet but now with claws.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may be building this up a bit more than the book does. There aren't really examples of what the Cult considers pure and what they consider enough. Especially considering that we already have a number of tribes that consider really messed up things as normal. One might argue that their methods might be cleaner than the ones of the say plaguebringer Red Talon. Mostly because the book is so intent on telling us they are badwrong without actually giving us some examples and erring on the side of nazism/fascism in the adventures.<br /> <br /> This applies to the Black Spiral Dancers, too. What do they actually do? Why are they a threat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T12:47:53-08:00","id":1528825,"title":"","content":"I would very much agree that any advice on the CoF as they currently are should include advocating for coming up with how to separate the CoF and the BSDs as antagonists in a meaningful way, because W5 so far hasn't done so. While not something to necessarily copy directly, Forsaken has the Pure (werewolves that actually agree with a lot of things that the PCs believe in, but have a few really big disagreements that have festered into generations of violent conflict), and the Bale Hounds (straight up evil werewolves that sold their souls, but are also very good at hiding who they really are until they get you to sign on the line too). Two different enemy werewolf groups, and even ones that might engage with a lot of similar activities, but thematically very different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T14:42:39-08:00","id":1528831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528825#post1528825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would very much agree that any advice on the CoF as they currently are should include advocating for coming up with how to separate the CoF and the BSDs as antagonists in a meaningful way, because W5 so far hasn't done so. While not something to necessarily copy directly, Forsaken has the Pure (werewolves that actually agree with a lot of things that the PCs believe in, but have a few really big disagreements that have festered into generations of violent conflict), and the Bale Hounds (straight up evil werewolves that sold their souls, but are also very good at hiding who they really are until they get you to sign on the line too). Two different enemy werewolf groups, and even ones that might engage with a lot of similar activities, but thematically very different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it's a pretty easy to separate group.<br /> <br /> 1. BSDs are Wyrm tainted crazy serial killers and Texas Chainsaw Massacre inbred &quot;overtly evil&quot; monsters. Doctor Satan and Michael Meyers.<br /> <br /> 2. The Cult of Fenris are a bunch of crazy Pro-Gaia fanatics who murder people because they think they're doing God's work to save the planet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T14:55:41-08:00","id":1528832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528831#post1528831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2. The Cult of Fenris are a bunch of crazy Pro-Gaia fanatics who murder people because they think they're doing God's work to save the planet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean from the outside most people describe all Garou that way. Trying to cut back on it kind of tips the Garou away from being frightening horror monsters, and putting it on a scale where one side knocks your character out of your control just seems counter to the game, making the other (starting) side way too &quot;safe&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T15:31:49-08:00","id":1528835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528832#post1528832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean from the outside most people describe all Garou that way. Trying to cut back on it kind of tips the Garou away from being frightening horror monsters, and putting it on a scale where one side knocks your character out of your control just seems counter to the game, making the other (starting) side way too &quot;safe&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I thought that was kind of the point. The Get of Fenris becoming the Cult of Fenris was the logical endpoint of the typical philosophy of, &quot;Grrr, Wyrmspawn, kill!&quot;<br /> <br /> And seeing how pointless and futile it is as well as self=defeating with the Cult helps the Garou go, &quot;hold up a minute. Do I sound like that?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T16:11:22-08:00","id":1528839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528835#post1528835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, I thought that was kind of the point. The Get of Fenris becoming the Cult of Fenris was the logical endpoint of the typical philosophy of, &quot;Grrr, Wyrmspawn, kill!&quot;<br /> <br /> And seeing how pointless and futile it is as well as self=defeating with the Cult helps the Garou go, &quot;hold up a minute. Do I sound like that?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Leveling that as a criticism, however, is usually done by people who are really dismissive of the Garou's mission. The kind of people who think that BSDs are literally the Garou's version of the Sabbat, second guess everything about the game, reject its premise, and ultimately make a fifth edition that's devoid of everything important in the game while dismissing all of the past editions as &quot;legacy&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T16:16:48-08:00","id":1528841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528839#post1528839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Leveling that as a criticism, however, is usually done by people who are really dismissive of the Garou's mission. The kind of people who think that BSDs are literally the Garou's version of the Sabbat, second guess everything about the game, reject its premise, and ultimately make a fifth edition that's devoid of everything important in the game while dismissing all of the past editions as &quot;legacy&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's been a central premise of the game from the very beginning that unquestioning acceptance of the Garou's mission is wrong and stupid. I mean, that's why Evan the White Savior Boy exists. The Impergium, War of Rage, The Bunyip, The War in the Amazon (which is War of Rage 2.0 or implying it never really stopped), and so on. None of the ideas presented in W5 are &quot;new&quot; and have been there from the very beginning.<br /> <br /> Which is why the whole &quot;dismiss Legacy&quot; thing is so fucking weird to me. They in fact make a lot more sense with the history of the game's canon backing them up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T16:48:47-08:00","id":1528842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528841#post1528841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, it's been a central premise of the game from the very beginning that unquestioning acceptance of the Garou's mission is wrong and stupid. I mean, that's why Evan the White Savior Boy exists. The Impergium, War of Rage, The Bunyip, The War in the Amazon (which is War of Rage 2.0 or implying it never really stopped), and so on. None of the ideas presented in W5 are &quot;new&quot; and have been there from the very beginning.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... not it at all. The central premise of the game is that the modern garou have to somehow avert the apocalypse, because their ancestors spent precious time doing stuff OTHER than their mission.<br /> <br /> The Nation's mission is to fight the Wyrm to prevent it from spreading and corrupting things.<br /> <br /> What the Nation did INSTEAD was to question their fellow shifters, then each other and they spent all the time they had preventing the Wyrm from spreading fighting each other and creating massive rifts between tribes. Nevermind other shifters. The Howlers fell because no one came to their aid, the Bunyip were killed because a Red Talon could not accept them as garou.<br /> <br /> So when modern days came to pass, the Nation collectively looked up from their sandbox and went &quot;oops.&quot;<br /> <br /> The basic premise of the game is that the PCs must untangle the Nation from this state of internal issues and actually focus on fighting the Wyrm.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T16:58:19-08:00","id":1528843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528842#post1528842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's... not it at all. The central premise of the game is that the modern garou have to somehow avert the apocalypse, because their ancestors spent precious time doing stuff OTHER than their mission.<br /> <br /> The Nation's mission is to fight the Wyrm to prevent it from spreading and corrupting things.<br /> <br /> What the Nation did INSTEAD was to question their fellow shifters, then each other and they spent all the time they had preventing the Wyrm from spreading fighting each other and creating massive rifts between tribes. Nevermind other shifters. The Howlers fell because no one came to their aid, the Bunyip were killed because a Red Talon could not accept them as garou.<br /> <br /> So when modern days came to pass, the Nation collectively looked up from their sandbox and went &quot;oops.&quot;<br /> <br /> The basic premise of the game is that the PCs must untangle the Nation from this state of internal issues and actually focus on fighting the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was always my takeaway. The Garou fucked up because they started focusing on stuff other than their mission. In their hubris they wiped out the other Shifters, and then they were so busy trying to cover for all of the roles that the other Shifters would have filled that they ended up taking their focus off of fighting the Wyrm which allowed the Wyrm to grow far stronger than it otherwise would have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T17:01:01-08:00","id":1528847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528841#post1528841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, it's been a central premise of the game from the very beginning that unquestioning acceptance of the Garou's mission is wrong and stupid. I mean, that's why Evan the White Savior Boy exists. The Impergium, War of Rage, The Bunyip, The War in the Amazon (which is War of Rage 2.0 or implying it never really stopped), and so on. None of the ideas presented in W5 are &quot;new&quot; and have been there from the very beginning.<br /> <br /> Which is why the whole &quot;dismiss Legacy&quot; thing is so fucking weird to me. They in fact make a lot more sense with the history of the game's canon backing them up.</div> </div> </div> </div>... you mean the whole War of the Amazon that brought the highest of the elders of the <b>Get of Fenris</b> to bend knee for the Changing Breeds of the Amazon and start cooperating with them. The War for the Amazon that ended up with the Shadow Lords seeking atonement for their part in the death of the Camatotz by bringing back a part of Bat itself from the Wyrm and possibly even the breed? That &quot;War of Rage 2.0 ?&quot; Even in the original book the point was that the Garou there were misguided rather than genocidal. Half the plot hooks were about forging forward with the Fera.<br /> <br /> Also, fuck Evan. He was well intended, but Native Americans don't need a White Savior. The Younger Brother was defined by their Rage and the insult done upon them and their people by the Wyrmcomers. An element of their growth is learning to pick their battles and accept that they need allies to make a change. One of their own spearheading that would have been vastly superior to Dances-With-The-Wolves.<br /> <br /> The Garou mission is neither wrong nor stupid, and only someone who doesn't understand what their mission actually is can spout such gibberish. Garou are here to make sure that the world lives on one more day. They were supposed to do better, and while they did great things to keep the world going, they fucked up quite a few times. Now there's no more time for fuckups and its time to live up to what they were made for.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T17:01:28-08:00","id":1528848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528843#post1528843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that was always my takeaway. The Garou fucked up because they started focusing on stuff other than their mission. In their hubris they wiped out the other Shifters, and then they were so busy trying to cover for all of the roles that the other Shifters would have filled that they ended up taking their focus off of fighting the Wyrm which allowed the Wyrm to grow far stronger than it otherwise would have.</div> </div> </div> </div>By contrast, my take on it was always, &quot;The Children of Gaia and Stargazers have it right.&quot;<br /> <br /> For me, the issue was that fighting the Wyrm was not the solution because the Wyrm was a threat that could only be defeated by healing/teaching humanity. That may have been something the werebears and Mokole were supposed to do.<br /> <br /> So a large part of the subtext was figuring out how to be less Ahroun and more Philodox and Galiard and Ragabash.<br /> <br /> Monkeywrenchers was one of the rare cases where Garou actually found a new way to do it and the assumption was the Glass Walker Hackers were probably causing more harm to Pentex than the rest of the nation combined.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528847#post1528847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... you mean the whole War of the Amazon that brought the highest of the elders of the <b>Get of Fenris</b> to bend knee for the Changing Breeds of the Amazon and start cooperating with them. The War for the Amazon that ended up with the Shadow Lords seeking atonement for their part in the death of the Camatotz by bringing back a part of Bat itself from the Wyrm and possibly even the breed? That &quot;War of Rage 2.0 ?&quot; Even in the original book the point was that the Garou there were misguided rather than genocidal. Half the plot hooks were about forging forward with the Fera.<br /> <br /> Also, fuck Evan. He was well intended, but Native Americans don't need a White Savior. The Younger Brother was defined by their Rage and the insult done upon them and their people by the Wyrmcomers. An element of their growth is learning to pick their battles and accept that they need allies to make a change. One of their own spearheading that would have been vastly superior to Dances-With-The-Wolves.<br /> <br /> The Garou mission is neither wrong nor stupid, and only someone who doesn't understand what their mission actually is can spout such gibberish. Garou are here to make sure that the world lives on one more day. They were supposed to do better, and while they did great things to keep the world going, they fucked up quite a few times. Now there's no more time for fuckups and its time to live up to what they were made for.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Random Aside:<br /> <br /> If I was allowed to rewrite Evan, I'd have him be actually Native American but he got stolen from his family by a crooked adoption service of the kind that still exist. Basically raised by a white family and not even knowing that he'd been kidnapped and robbed of his heritage. It would actually go a long way to making him genuinely relevant. His goal would be to find out his actual past that was stolen from him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-18-2024, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T17:18:22-08:00","id":1528853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528848#post1528848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By contrast, my take on it was always, &quot;The Children of Gaia and Stargazers have it right.&quot;<br /> <br /> For me, the issue was that fighting the Wyrm was not the solution because the Wyrm was a threat that could only be defeated by healing/teaching humanity. That may have been something the werebears and Mokole were supposed to do.<br /> <br /> So a large part of the subtext was figuring out how to be less Ahroun and more Philodox and Galiard and Ragabash.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fighting the Wyrm WAS a solution, for the garou and the ajaba. That was their job. But they decided to try and rule over others, something which wasn't their job. Cue this mess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528848#post1528848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Monkeywrenchers was one of the rare cases where Garou actually found a new way to do it and the assumption was the Glass Walker Hackers were probably causing more harm to Pentex than the rest of the nation combined.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, there should not be the need for monkeywrenchers. There should be no Pentex. These were things the garou could have avoided IF they had focused on fighting the Wyrm and not on personal grudges.<br /> <br /> The Monkeywrenchers are only needed because the fight is now so fractured and massive that they have to find new ways to figure things out.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T17:25:42-08:00","id":1528856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528853#post1528853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, there should not be the need for monkeywrenchers. There should be no Pentex. These were things the garou could have avoided IF they had focused on fighting the Wyrm and not on personal grudges.<br /> <br /> The Monkeywrenchers are only needed because the fight is now so fractured and massive that they have to find new ways to figure things out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, the enemy evolved and the Garou had to evolve with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T17:46:04-08:00","id":1528858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528848#post1528848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By contrast, my take on it was always, &quot;The Children of Gaia and Stargazers have it right.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very first edition way to think of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For me, the issue was that fighting the Wyrm was not the solution because the Wyrm was a threat that could only be defeated by healing/teaching humanity. That may have been something the werebears and Mokole were supposed to do. </div> </div> </div>You won't be able to heal humanity if you don't take up arms against the very direct enemies that still exist. This creates a multi-front war, however, and that's never good for the side that's surrounded.<br /> <br /> Also guidance of humanity was the Apis (long since dead; the minotaur Asterion in Knossos was supposedly the last, and with the domestication of cattle and death of the last aurochs, they're out and not necessarily just by Garou hands). Mokole could have caused humanity to forget the Impergium more effectively, but they wouldn't, because recall that they kind of did something worse to make humanity out of ancestral pre-humans in the first place, having been present to carve them over a few tens of millions of years into something more like the Kings.<br /> <br /> Turns out that the Garou aren't the only one that makes terrible, terrible mistakes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So a large part of the subtext was figuring out how to be less Ahroun and more Philodox and Galiard and Ragabash. </div> </div> </div>Why leave out the Theurges?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Monkeywrenchers was one of the rare cases where Garou actually found a new way to do it and the assumption was the Glass Walker Hackers were probably causing more harm to Pentex than the rest of the nation combined. </div> </div> </div>Let's flip this on its head and make it about humans doing monkeywrenching. Note that on teams of saboteurs, like in Shadowrun or Cyberpunk in the appropriate vein (i.e. not working for the corpos) not everyone has the same talents, and not everyone has a temperament that allows for perfect infiltration via social engineering, working computers, etc. Just as with the human team, a Garou pack is not going to have the same personal proclivities between every member (beyond what their patron might grant them), so screaming about people that are violent needing to be less violent is missing the point.<br /> <br /> You need the violence people, still, quite likely now more than ever. You just need other people to help them get where they need to fully freak out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T17:46:22-08:00","id":1528859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528856#post1528856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, the enemy evolved and the Garou had to evolve with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The enemy evolved because the garou had the chance to stop it, but they were too busy fighting over caerns to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T18:04:05-08:00","id":1528861,"title":"","content":"But fighting the actual Wyrm and his followers was never the problem, nor was it ever depicted as anything other than the right thing for the Garou to be doing. If anything, it's always been portrayed as direct action. Sure, it was also important to educate humanity and guide them into doing better, but the Garou weren't shown as wrong for physically trying to stop a thing that's actively trying to destroy the planet. The problems came when they got sidetracked into infighting or accusing things of being &quot;wyrm-tainted&quot; that weren't, both with the Fera and themselves. The solution put forward before to remember who the real enemy is and what they're all actually fighting for, and actually work to make right what their forbears did wrong, not sit around in their little corners of the world doing absolutely nothing while angsting about how much their ancestors sucked like W5 seems to put forward.<br /> <br /> If anything, W5 seems to suggest that the answer is <i>more</i> of this infighting, seeing as it constantly implies &quot;but is the Wyrm reeeeally that bad? Is fighting to save the planet reeeeeally the right thing to do?&quot; and trying to push the Cult of Fenris, a group that fundamentally wants the same thing that is the Garou's born purpose, as the Big Bads. And has an entire mechanic based around the idea that caring too much is a fast-track to being a fascist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T18:20:23-08:00","id":1528862,"title":"","content":"I always imagined that Evan's family probably had some American Indian heritage. There are plenty of white families in America that have an Indian ancestor in their family tree even if they aren't on some tribal register or consider themselves Indian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T18:26:55-08:00","id":1528864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528862#post1528862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always imagined that Evan's family probably had some American Indian heritage. There are plenty of white families in America that have an Indian ancestor in their family tree even if they aren't on some tribal register or consider themselves Indian.</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to remember a comment that the writing team were unhappy with how 'white suburban' the comic artist depicted Evan, which unfortunately set the tone for all future depictions of him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T18:58:11-08:00","id":1528865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528864#post1528864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I seem to remember a comment that the writing team were unhappy with how 'white suburban' the comic artist depicted Evan, which unfortunately set the tone for all future depictions of him.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean they could have had some wiggle room until the character description straight up said he didn't look like he had any Native American heritage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T20:50:29-08:00","id":1528870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528848#post1528848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By contrast, my take on it was always, &quot;The Children of Gaia and Stargazers have it right.&quot;<br /> <br /> For me, the issue was that fighting the Wyrm was not the solution because the Wyrm was a threat that could only be defeated by healing/teaching humanity. That may have been something the werebears and Mokole were supposed to do.<br /> <br /> So a large part of the subtext was figuring out how to be less Ahroun and more Philodox and Galiard and Ragabash.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was a big point of the game. The Wyrm wasn't the only foe, there was also the Weaver and the werewolves just weren't really capable of dealing with it but were stuck with it. Being a raging war machine doesn't really work in destroying the Weaver's tools the way it does the Wyrm's tools. The Wyrm adopting the Weaver's tools was basically the beginning of the end for the werewolves because they just weren't made to fight against that. <br /> <br /> And yeah, bringing the old shifters together and healing the wounds of the past was pretty important - look at what happened in the metaplot with Australia or in Africa or in the Amazon. Getting the other shifters to work with the werewolves was a big focus as the game went on. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T01:31:11-08:00","id":1528877,"title":"","content":"One thing that stands out is if the CoF are supposed to be Earth First Eco-Terrorists who are obsessed with saving Gaia at all costs.....then why are the humans they work with ( as depicted so far) Trumper/Alt-Right types rather than ALF or ELF members?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T01:58:25-08:00","id":1528879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528848#post1528848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By contrast, my take on it was always, &quot;The Children of Gaia and Stargazers have it right.&quot;<br /> <br /> For me, the issue was that fighting the Wyrm was not the solution because the Wyrm was a threat that could only be defeated by healing/teaching humanity. That may have been something the werebears and Mokole were supposed to do.<br /> <br /> So a large part of the subtext was figuring out how to be less Ahroun and more Philodox and Galiard and Ragabash.<br /> <br /> Monkeywrenchers was one of the rare cases where Garou actually found a new way to do it and the assumption was the Glass Walker Hackers were probably causing more harm to Pentex than the rest of the nation combined.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Fighting the Wyrm is not the solution&quot; goes way too far. You're losing sight of the actual game at that point. There are thematic considerations in terms of roleplaying and worldbuilding like the tragedy of the Garou and atoning for their mistakes but that isn't the focus of the game: fighting the Wyrm is the focus of the game. That's the point of making Garou these combat-machines via their Forms and Rage while being a double-edged sword is still a sword that is a tool to use in the fight against the Wyrm. The tag-line of the game is &quot;When will you Rage?&quot; and while the game cares about Garou learning from the mistakes of the past to fight smarter, not harder, the fighting is very much the center of attention in terms of mechanics. The Fomori are there to be fought, Pentex is there to be fought and the Wyrm is there to be fought and opposed.<br /> <br /> If you go too negative on what Garou can accomplish and too pessimistic on the war against the Wyrm, well... then you have rendered the game pointless. For example, if you're so pessimistic about what Garou can do that you think any hacker using their computer-skills is more worthwhile &quot;than the rest of the Nation combined&quot; then you've just destroyed the game. The main-tools the game revolves around are Rage, the Gifts, Rites and the Forms. If you're going at this with the assumption that all of that is nothing compared to somebody who put four or five dots in Computers then you're just wasting the players' time with that approach. This isn't a game designed to be about hacking a corporation and so any perspective that is too negative just loses sight of what the actual game is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T02:41:42-08:00","id":1528882,"title":"","content":"OK, to try to get back to what I meant a bit here:<br /> <br /> The problem with the CoF in the books, and the BSDs in the books, is that they are ultimately the same kind of antagonists with different window dressing: evil extremists werewolves that can't actually be reasoned with and trying only diminishes you.<br /> <br /> Fighting Jason Vorhees, Michael Myres, and Leatherface are all different in the details, but there's a reason why those stories get very similar as time has gone on. The originals had some unique quirks to them, but once those quirks fade into repeats for sequels, they turn into the same antagonist with different window dressing. They're variations on a them, which is what leads us to having and idea of what a hulking brute slasher archetype is in the first place.<br /> <br /> As applies to W5 specifically, consider how &quot;pulp action hero punches Nazis,&quot; is a very common thing, but, &quot;pulp action hero punches Mussolini's blackshirts,&quot; isn't. Were the Italian fascists allied with the German fascists somehow a different sort of evil? Not really. The Nazis just make for better pop-culture villains: the experimental technology they kept investing in to try to find a weapon that would change the course of the war, the weird occultist submovement within them, the &quot;mystery&quot; of Hilter's body never being &quot;confirmed.&quot; The narrative around the Nazis just makes for better larger than life story fodder that makes them different from just waging a justified war against a horrific strain of authoritarian assholes.<br /> <br /> W5 has the same problem: The CoF got all the stuff to make them interesting, while the BSDs are just... there because that part of the legacy wasn't removed. Who either group says their fighting for is irrelevant to what kind of stories you can use them for when they fight the same way, and their means is vastly more important to their role as narrative devices than their ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T02:55:06-08:00","id":1528883,"title":"","content":"And also<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528848#post1528848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By contrast, my take on it was always, &quot;The Children of Gaia and Stargazers have it right.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Both those tribes still fight the Wyrm. That is a thing they do. I get where you're coming from in that they also focus on education/healing/all that, but they still do very much fight the Wyrm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T04:09:07-08:00","id":1528887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528738#post1528738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Albrecht is mentioned on page 190 in the Silver Crown entry.<br /> <br /> As a symbol of its grandeur, the Silver Fangs<br /> tribe exalts the Silver Crown, a legendary artifact<br /> belonging to the Albrecht lineage of Silver Fang<br /> werewolves. With the disappearance of the last<br /> proclaimed king of the tribe, however, two great<br /> icons of tribal esteem have been lost, which many<br /> Garou interpret as an omen about the fate of the<br /> Silver Fangs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't it be just an easter egg?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T04:38:32-08:00","id":1528888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528848#post1528848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By contrast, my take on it was always, &quot;The Children of Gaia and Stargazers have it right.&quot;<br /> <br /> For me, the issue was that fighting the Wyrm was not the solution because the Wyrm was a threat that could only be defeated by healing/teaching humanity. That may have been something the werebears and Mokole were supposed to do.<br /> <br /> So a large part of the subtext was figuring out how to be less Ahroun and more Philodox and Galiard and Ragabash.<br /> <br /> Monkeywrenchers was one of the rare cases where Garou actually found a new way to do it and the assumption was the Glass Walker Hackers were probably causing more harm to Pentex than the rest of the nation combined.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your lack of Werewolf experience is showing again. You fight the Wyrm in all the shapes and forms. Many (if not most) of those forms are not fightable with tooth and claw. These things that you list as exceptions have been standards, and the published history of the Garou is loaded with different methodologies to counteract the Apocalypse, recruit allies, make amends and generally live up to the potential they were made for. It was a hallmark of the 1st edition that the Garou were lost and finding their way, most of 2nd and Revised were about the Garou being Vibrant and on the move - making changes and finding new and better methods to make sure that something is done before it's too late.<br /> <br /> Garou society relies on there being five auspices and all of them doing their jobs. If they are all being Ahrouns, something is wrong. Thankfully, the books were quite clear that the Garou are not all Ahrouns and that they are able to do more than just rend and maim. Contrary to what the average person seems to construe as the typical Werewolf MO and how the game is just about fighting (&quot;Similar to D&amp;D&quot;).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T05:16:53-08:00","id":1528890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528877#post1528877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that stands out is if the CoF are supposed to be Earth First Eco-Terrorists who are obsessed with saving Gaia at all costs.....then why are the humans they work with ( as depicted so far) Trumper/Alt-Right types rather than ALF or ELF members?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because the Cult of Fenris will kill anyone who doesn't provide unquestioned obedience to their leadership. Again, it boils down to the fact that anything actually USEFUL is going to be done by the Garou Nation.<br /> <br /> Protests. Monkey wrenching. Bribery at the highest levels.<br /> <br /> The depiction of the Cult is that their violent action now philosophy is meant to be counter productive and useless. Which I think is a weird subtext because some fans seem to want to think the Cult have the right idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gh0st-fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528883#post1528883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And also<br /> <br /> Both those tribes still fight the Wyrm. That is a thing they do. I get where you're coming from in that they also focus on education/healing/all that, but they still do very much fight the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point being the goal is to &quot;Save Gaia&quot; not &quot;Beat Sauron.&quot; I think the game went overboard but people also act like it said that the Garou aren't still doing their fighting Endron, Pentex, Banes, and so on business that they always were.<br /> <br /> When they manifestly are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-19-2024, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T05:20:19-08:00","id":1528891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-fo