chments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T05:24:29-08:00","id":1528892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528891#post1528891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Short response: These kind of comments don't encourage me to continue participating.<br /> <br /> Just how many campaigns do I have to run to qualify to respond?<br /> <br /> Quick question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't set the threshold at a number of campaigns, but I would expect a better grasp of the material and its evolution rather than the number of contextual errors you've been making in representing what was in the old material and what is in the new material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T05:39:01-08:00","id":1528893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528891#post1528891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Short response: These kind of comments don't encourage me to continue participating.<br /> <br /> Just how many campaigns do I have to run to qualify to respond?<br /> <br /> Quick question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know the question wasn't meant for me, but I'll answer anyway, I think it has more to do with quality than quantity, you could play one session a week for 20 years in full-ahroun mode with the same players and someone else could do the same for just 1 or 2 years exploring details of the lore and having other types of approaches, that said, I think you understand where I'm going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T05:42:05-08:00","id":1528895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528892#post1528892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't set the threshold at a number of campaigns, but I would expect a better grasp of the material and its evolution rather than the number of contextual errors you've been making in representing what was in the old material and what is in the new material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well then, I understand and you can ignore any of my future posts.<br /> <br /> I will be continuing to respond to threads, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T05:42:38-08:00","id":1528896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528882#post1528882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W5 has the same problem: The CoF got all the stuff to make them interesting, while the BSDs are just... there because that part of the legacy wasn't removed. Who either group says their fighting for is irrelevant to what kind of stories you can use them for when they fight the same way, and their means is vastly more important to their role as narrative devices than their ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention, if we are to respect the RAW, the way these two bad guy factions are used has to change wildly from Legacy.<br /> <br /> In The Deepest Wounds, the good sept doesn't do anything as the CoF go and fight the Wyrm. No matter how you slice it, that sounds silly and like they don't care.<br /> <br /> The RAW of W5 is that the Litany is obeyed selectively, there is no Nation but some elders and some isolated septs, there are no kinfolk to handle mundane matters and aid in running the Nation and that the PCs are largely on their own.<br /> <br /> In Legacy, if a Caern was becoming tainted and the news got out, the Nation would muster war parties, talismans and temporary packs in a few days. In W5, if you hear a caern is getting tainted? You'd have to truly weigh your options on whether you could risk it or should you just hope the sept there wouldn't affect you. Because you have no higher authority to contact, you have no network of kin to use and local Elders might think leaving your caern to fight another is worthy of taking it over.<br /> <br /> In such a setting, the way BSDs function is going to be radically different from Legacy. That is why I think they should be the most structured tribe, the one with the power in the age of apocalypse. No longer hiding in underground hives, now they can do whatever they want. And since the PCs aren't as beholden to the Litany as before, there is a strong incentive to let them to protect your own hide. It takes a lot of guts to fight back and take down a BSD pack, but then you have actually done something great by protecting your area.<br /> <br /> For the CoF, as I stated before, I don't want to focus on them vs what remains of the Nation. I want to focus on the meatgrinder of their existence. Hauglosk is still meant to be a sort of madness, so the tribe tries its best but is often running out of members due to them being a death cult and the enormity of their foes. So they try to get worthy garou to fill their ranks, or try to take over caerns in places they think are strategically important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T05:50:09-08:00","id":1528897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528895#post1528895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well then, I understand and you can ignore any of my future posts.<br /> <br /> I will be continuing to respond to threads, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'll be happy to correct you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T05:50:21-08:00","id":1528898,"title":"","content":"Saying, &quot;Don't fight the Wyrm&quot; requires whoever says I'm saying that to not actually be reading my responses but we know that. The examples given are where the Garou Nation showing how badly they've done it and mistakes they've made in believing wiping out the werebears was &quot;fighting the Wyrm.&quot; So was the Impergium. So was the War in the Amazon (which as mentioned was supposed to have ended on a high note but didn't change the fact the initial set up was Jaguars and Mokole vs. Garou vs. Pentex).<br /> <br /> I've mentioned multiple times the thing about W5 is it's not saying not to fight the Wyrm. It's saying that fighting the Wyrm isn't the mindset you should be having. It should be saving Gaia (if such is possible) or even if Gaia isn't savagable, then doing as much good as possible anyway. Harano is literally the state of doing nothing becaue it all seems so pointless. Now this is confusing but it's something that really appeals to me as it allows a lot of chances for angst as well as brooding.<br /> <br /> My earliest experience with Werewolf the Apocalypse was Under a Blood Red Moon where my PCs broke the treaty with the Gangrel immediately, slaughtered a bunch of cops, and generally behaved as the worst sort of Garou stereotypes (we were fourteen). They didn't fight intelligently or with diplomacy but &quot;Wyrm, Smash!&quot;<br /> <br /> And that's a fun game.<br /> <br /> Antiheroes for the win.<br /> <br /> But it makes it very easy to understand why the Cult of Fenris as a group of villains should exist to show the kind of mayhem the Garou were engaged in was not only counterproductive but outright evil. Where is the new line, though? That is a question the Garou have to figure out themselves and what is or is not justified in the quest to save Gaia or whatever is left?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T05:52:28-08:00","id":1528899,"title":"","content":"[Deleted -- my bad]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-19-2024, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T05:56:19-08:00","id":1528900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528896#post1528896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In such a setting, the way BSDs function is going to be radically different from Legacy. That is why I think they should be the most structured tribe, the one with the power in the age of apocalypse. No longer hiding in underground hives, now they can do whatever they want. And since the PCs aren't as beholden to the Litany as before, there is a strong incentive to let them to protect your own hide. It takes a lot of guts to fight back and take down a BSD pack, but then you have actually done something great by protecting your area.<br /> <br /> For the CoF, as I stated before, I don't want to focus on them vs what remains of the Nation. I want to focus on the meatgrinder of their existence. Hauglosk is still meant to be a sort of madness, so the tribe tries its best but is often running out of members due to them being a death cult and the enormity of their foes. So they try to get worthy garou to fill their ranks, or try to take over caerns in places they think are strategically important.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, if I was the line developer for W5, I would probably go in an interesting direction for the Black Spiral Dancers which is the fact that this isn't working out for them either. They believe the Howl is the death of Gaia but...nothing has changed. There has been no great reward, no hordes of Hell invading things, and no freedom of the Wyrm from the Weaver. There's a lot of interesting directions to go with the Black Spiral Dancer that can still leave them as a bunch of murderous thugs but also potentially having their own crisis of faith.<br /> <br /> Bluntly, the Wyrm isn't winning.<br /> <br /> The Weaver has.<br /> <br /> Assuming either cares in the slightest about all of this.<br /> <br /> But yes, the BSD should be suffering Hauglosk and Harano like the Garou are. Maybe also their own civil wars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T06:01:40-08:00","id":1528901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528890#post1528890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably because the Cult of Fenris will kill anyone who doesn't provide unquestioned obedience to their leadership. Again, it boils down to the fact that anything actually USEFUL is going to be done by the Garou Nation.<br /> <br /> Protests. Monkey wrenching. Bribery at the highest levels.<br /> <br /> The depiction of the Cult is that their violent action now philosophy is meant to be counter productive and useless. Which I think is a weird subtext because some fans seem to want to think the Cult have the right idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because what they are doing is what the Legacy game said was the right thing; Don't worry about internal conflict and focus on fighting the Wyrm. While the remnants of the Nation are written as NOT doing that because that is bad and what the CoF do.<br /> <br /> Nevermind that the W5 setting literally doesn't have the ways to do what could be done in Legacy.<br /> <br /> Also, I think you should dial back a bit and consider what you just said were the ways to really fight for Gaia. <b>&quot;Protests. Monkey wrenching. Bribery at the highest levels.&quot; </b>Things that a normal human can already do. Even if you don't intend it, you keep saying that the way to play the game called WEREWOLF the Apocalypse is to not play a werewolf or engage with werewolf mechanics. You are also constantly ignoring that the fight is not only physical but spiritual as well.<br /> <br /> Garou are made to punch the spirit of cancer out of someone, especially in W5 where Rage is even more volatile, that is what they do at their best. That the W5 core treats this as the worst choice is bad writing, because it says you shouldn't engage with its core mechanics.<br /> <br /> If you want a game where the focus is on those three things you listed as good, you can do that better by playing a human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T06:07:58-08:00","id":1528902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528898#post1528898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying, &quot;Don't fight the Wyrm&quot; requires whoever says I'm saying that to not actually be reading my responses but we know that.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you literally said that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For me, the issue was that fighting the Wyrm was not the solution because the Wyrm was a threat that could only be defeated by healing/teaching humanity. That may have been something the werebears and Mokole were supposed to do. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T06:13:34-08:00","id":1528903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528898#post1528898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying, &quot;Don't fight the Wyrm&quot; requires whoever says I'm saying that to not actually be reading my responses but we know that. The examples given are where the Garou Nation showing how badly they've done it and mistakes they've made in believing wiping out the werebears was &quot;fighting the Wyrm.&quot; So was the Impergium. So was the War in the Amazon (which as mentioned was supposed to have ended on a high note but didn't change the fact the initial set up was Jaguars and Mokole vs. Garou vs. Pentex).<br /> <br /> I've mentioned multiple times the thing about W5 is it's not saying not to fight the Wyrm. It's saying that fighting the Wyrm isn't the mindset you should be having. It should be saving Gaia (if such is possible) or even if Gaia isn't savagable, then doing as much good as possible anyway. Harano is literally the state of doing nothing becaue it all seems so pointless. Now this is confusing but it's something that really appeals to me as it allows a lot of chances for angst as well as brooding.<br /> <br /> My earliest experience with Werewolf the Apocalypse was Under a Blood Red Moon where my PCs broke the treaty with the Gangrel immediately, slaughtered a bunch of cops, and generally behaved as the worst sort of Garou stereotypes (we were fourteen). They didn't fight intelligently or with diplomacy but &quot;Wyrm, Smash!&quot;<br /> <br /> And that's a fun game.<br /> <br /> Antiheroes for the win.<br /> <br /> But it makes it very easy to understand why the Cult of Fenris as a group of villains should exist to show the kind of mayhem the Garou were engaged in was not only counterproductive but outright evil. Where is the new line, though? That is a question the Garou have to figure out themselves and what is or is not justified in the quest to save Gaia or whatever is left?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and it's a good outline that explains the bad writing in the W5 corebook. It all culminates in &quot;Where is the new line, though?&quot; and the game has absolutely no answer to that. Everything got rejected. Garou-Nation. Fallen. The Litany. Just sucks and gets exploited constantly. Umbra. Dangerous and pretty inaccessible. Gaia. Dead/Dying. The Apocalypse. It's here and can't be stopped. Garou. All doomed to fall to Harano or Hauglosk at some point.<br /> <br /> So where is that new line even supposed to come from...? Because you can reject all those things and make the game about that very new line. But W5 is not about that. You're still a Garou, you still chase Renown, you're still supposed to deal with spirits even though the Umbra has become more dangerous and inaccessible, you still hang around in Septs, you deal with caerns, when you encounter Wyrm-minion, Fomori, Bane-spirits, you still in the end just fight them (there's no revelatory alternate path within the game) and Harano and Hauglosk are these damocles-swords hanging over the head of your character that you can't escape from.<br /> <br /> W5 doesn't have an answer to what the &quot;new line&quot; is even supposed to be. Or comes even close to suggesting how there can be a &quot;new line&quot; in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T06:16:02-08:00","id":1528904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528901#post1528901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably because what they are doing is what the Legacy game said was the right thing; Don't worry about internal conflict and focus on fighting the Wyrm. While the remnants of the Nation are written as NOT doing that because that is bad and what the CoF do.<br /> <br /> Nevermind that the W5 setting literally doesn't have the ways to do what could be done in Legacy.<br /> <br /> Also, I think you should dial back a bit and consider what you just said were the ways to really fight for Gaia. <b>&quot;Protests. Monkey wrenching. Bribery at the highest levels.&quot; </b>Things that a normal human can already do. Even if you don't intend it, you keep saying that the way to play the game called WEREWOLF the Apocalypse is to not play a werewolf or engage with werewolf mechanics. You are also constantly ignoring that the fight is not only physical but spiritual as well.<br /> <br /> Garou are made to punch the spirit of cancer out of someone, especially in W5 where Rage is even more volatile, that is what they do at their best. That the W5 core treats this as the worst choice is bad writing, because it says you shouldn't engage with its core mechanics.<br /> <br /> If you want a game where the focus is on those three things you listed as good, you can do that better by playing a human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weirdly, I have an actual response to this.<br /> <br /> &quot;What do werewolves have to save Gaia that humans don't?&quot;<br /> <br /> Answer: &quot;Superpowers.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Garou can't beat the Wyrm with claws and attempting to do so has failed from probably the 20th century onward. Basically, once Pentex got involved, the Garou lost the war. At least with their current methodology. Its certainly FUN to go on a murder spree through Endron oil in EARTHBLOOD but I don't think anyone can argue that Cahill was making significant progress against Endron that way.<br /> <br /> Instead, I *REALLY LIKED* Heart of the Forest and the fact that you can achieve your mission via protests, sabotage, and behind the scene work but the ending of the story has you find out that a Formori is going to sabotage all your efforts and you have to figure out whether to kill the guy or not.<br /> <br /> If you're a Werewolf and want to do things other than claw things. What do you do?<br /> <br /> * Use Rites to cleanse areas with magic.<br /> * Go into the Umbra and slay the Bane of Pollution or whatnot so all of the oil damage or chemical waste dissolves in the real world (which I assume is what happens unless more is poured into the river)<br /> * Fight the supernatural goons that the baddies are sending against you. The WOD is a comic book so while Roxxon Oil can only be beaten by Tony Stark money or the government, that doesn't mean Roxxon isn't sending the Rhino to kill protestors.<br /> * Put a Glass Walker keyfob that will sort through all of the information in a hacking tool because MAGIC. Making hacking like it is in movies.<br /> And so on.<br /> <br /> Basically, SPIDER-MAN: MILES MORALES is a Werewolf: the Apocalypse game. Miles Morales and Phin both want to stop Roxxon Oil from putting up their toxic nuclear reactors in Harlem that will kill thousands of people over the next few years but they will continue to build because they make more money than they'll pay out in wrongful deaths.<br /> <br /> Phin wants to blow up Roxxon's HQ and kill people but this just helps Roxxon look like heroes in the public eye. Miles Morales' mother works with the politics while Miles struggles to get the information they need to expose Roxxon in the public and fights the Rhino and otrher supervillains while sabotaging their work.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T06:17:13-08:00","id":1528905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gh0st-fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528902#post1528902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But you literally said that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's not the solution because Gaia is dying is the problem not the Wyrm itself.<br /> <br /> You can't just claw the problem to death.<br /> <br /> Clawing the problem isn't USELESS but it isn't <i>enough</i>.<br /> <br /> That's my take at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T06:20:46-08:00","id":1528906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528903#post1528903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes and it's a good outline that explains the bad writing in the W5 corebook. It all culminates in &quot;Where is the new line, though?&quot; and the game has absolutely no answer to that. Everything got rejected. Garou-Nation. Fallen. The Litany. Just sucks and gets exploited constantly. Umbra. Dangerous and pretty inaccessible. Gaia. Dead/Dying. The Apocalypse. It's here and can't be stopped. Garou. All doomed to fall to Harano or Hauglosk at some point.<br /> <br /> So where is that new line even supposed to come from...? Because you can reject all those things and make the game about that very new line. But W5 is not about that. You're still a Garou, you still chase Renown, you're still supposed to deal with spirits even though the Umbra has become more dangerous and inaccessible, you still hang around in Septs, you deal with caerns, when you encounter Wyrm-minion, Fomori, Bane-spirits, you still in the end just fight them (there's no revelatory alternate path within the game) and Harano and Hauglosk are these damocles-swords hanging over the head of your character that you can't escape from.<br /> <br /> W5 doesn't have an answer to what the &quot;new line&quot; is even supposed to be. Or comes even close to suggesting how there can be a &quot;new line&quot; in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>...<br /> <br /> Yeah, you're right.<br /> <br /> I feel like the book really did a poor job of explaining what you SHOULD be doing while an excellent job of what they failed at.<br /> <br /> Questioning the Litany and giving no alternatives reminds me of the poor handling of the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> &quot;So, we agree that the laws of the Camarilla are bullshit, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;So...what's the new laws?&quot;<br /> <br /> *crickets chirp*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_bla