</div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The dog thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wolves do not closely resemble dogs. W5 is convinced otherwise, to the point of even describing not just Lupus as being hard to distinguish from a dog, but <i>Hispo</i> as looking like a big dog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T11:13:01-08:00","id":1528933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528931#post1528931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The dog thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hispo and Lupus forms are now said to resemble big dogs. Most likely so you can get away with using them in the city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T11:28:48-08:00","id":1528935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528933#post1528933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hispo and Lupus forms are now said to resemble big dogs. Most likely so you can get away with using them in the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like they could have easily gone with them having a mild delerium effect now.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T17:17:55-08:00","id":1528961,"title":"","content":"I had forgotten that detail about the dog.<br /> <br /> Well... the direction of this conversation reminded me of some things that seemed relevant to me and could even be used as a reference.<br /> <br /> In the Tribebook of the Black Furies pg 73 and 74 two rituals are mentioned: Mitigate the Scar and Fertility Ritual. The first is used to alleviate the pain of women and children who have suffered at the hands of their husbands or parents and thus begin the healing process; The second is, as the name suggests, it is a fertility ritual that returns fertility to those who have lost it, generally used on women, but it also works on men and wolves so you can see the possibilities. Doesn't work on Metis.<br /> <br /> In the Red Talons Tribebook pg 97: In the Legends section, the first one mentioned is, I don't know the exact name in English, stain glass, when a local church began cutting down the forest to build a road, her pack soon prepared to an attack, but in order to prevent a massacre she came up with a plan that involved dressing in stolen clothes and walking around the village attracting the attention of all the inhabitants, she attracted them to the chapel where she stained the glass with her blood and There she jumped into the Umbra leaving only her clothes, the village saw it as a miracle and kicked the people out of the church out of their lands. All things considered, she was pretty smart and avoided a massacre.<br /> <br /> In the Tribebook of Bone Gnawers pg 50: It is mentioned about Frankweilers who normally inhabit theaters, libraries and museums outside of working hours acting as their protectors, when one of these places is threatened they mobilize through protests, peaceful resistance, sabotage or umbral searches. An alternative is that they look for communities where they volunteer to teach people about languages, public health or the basics of medicine or law, basically anything that can be useful, they do this because the Wyrm tends to take advantage of the desperate and ignorant, so this would also be a way of fighting for Gaia.<br /> <br /> In the Glass Walkers' tribebook pg 63: They mention Urban farmers who find ways to make the Wyld proliferate in urban environments, whether through rituals or the use of technology, they even mention a sustainable growth project made by Asta Ljungdahl, an influential member of the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T18:07:56-08:00","id":1528968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528890#post1528890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably because the Cult of Fenris will kill anyone who doesn't provide unquestioned obedience to their leadership. .</div> </div> </div> </div>So where are they finding these people, why are they recruiting them, how are they keeping their loyalty, why are they using humans as footsoldiers and scouts, HOW the fuck are the Hauglosk eaten Rage-bombs even communicating or interacting with these people for more than a minute or so at a time?<br /> <br /> Because your statement above says they absolutely cannot interact with anyone Garou or Human who isn't a subordinate CoF without killing them.....which we know is untrue as the Hauglosk-filled CoF members in the Renegade material play somewhat subtle political games, kidnap and magically indoctrinate folks, cajole and convince and give chiminage and successfully interact with Gaian spirits all without killing anyone ( well, openly at least).<br /> <br /> Or are there members of the CoF that are unaffected by Hauglosk that do all the groundwork infiltration stuff without murderising everything in sight and others who do all the obey me or die death frenzy stuff. Kind of like the Legacy BSD ' normal seeming' recruiters vs the masses of physically corrupted Hive-dwellers that are too insane to do much more than kill everything in sight.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T18:12:41-08:00","id":1528970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528961#post1528961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had forgotten that detail about the dog.<br /> <br /> Well... the direction of this conversation reminded me of some things that seemed relevant to me and could even be used as a reference.<br /> <br /> In the Tribebook of the Black Furies pg 73 and 74 two rituals are mentioned: Mitigate the Scar and Fertility Ritual. The first is used to alleviate the pain of women and children who have suffered at the hands of their husbands or parents and thus begin the healing process; The second is, as the name suggests, it is a fertility ritual that returns fertility to those who have lost it, generally used on women, but it also works on men and wolves so you can see the possibilities. Doesn't work on Metis.<br /> <br /> In the Red Talons Tribebook pg 97: In the Legends section, the first one mentioned is, I don't know the exact name in English, stain glass, when a local church began cutting down the forest to build a road, her pack soon prepared to an attack, but in order to prevent a massacre she came up with a plan that involved dressing in stolen clothes and walking around the village attracting the attention of all the inhabitants, she attracted them to the chapel where she stained the glass with her blood and There she jumped into the Umbra leaving only her clothes, the village saw it as a miracle and kicked the people out of the church out of their lands. All things considered, she was pretty smart and avoided a massacre.<br /> <br /> In the Tribebook of Bone Gnawers pg 50: It is mentioned about Frankweilers who normally inhabit theaters, libraries and museums outside of working hours acting as their protectors, when one of these places is threatened they mobilize through protests, peaceful resistance, sabotage or umbral searches. An alternative is that they look for communities where they volunteer to teach people about languages, public health or the basics of medicine or law, basically anything that can be useful, they do this because the Wyrm tends to take advantage of the desperate and ignorant, so this would also be a way of fighting for Gaia.<br /> <br /> In the Glass Walkers' tribebook pg 63: They mention Urban farmers who find ways to make the Wyld proliferate in urban environments, whether through rituals or the use of technology, they even mention a sustainable growth project made by Asta Ljungdahl, an influential member of the group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there are literally hundreds of similar passages throughout Revised ( and some of early W20 before Paradox started fucking with it) of Garou building, assisting and actuating change through social movements and NGOs, admittedly usually with the buffer of Kinfolk so that things didn't get out of hand, with Packs providing support by taking care of threats or issues that were beyond the capabilities or perceptions of the humans and Kinfolk.<br /> <br /> And all of that got thrown away by W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T18:32:28-08:00","id":1528973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1528968#post1528968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So where are they finding these people, why are they recruiting them, how are they keeping their loyalty, why are they using humans as footsoldiers and scouts, HOW the fuck are the Hauglosk eaten Rage-bombs even communicating or interacting with these people for more than a minute or so at a time?<br /> <br /> Because your statement above says they absolutely cannot interact with anyone Garou or Human who isn't a subordinate CoF without killing them.....which we know is untrue as the Hauglosk-filled CoF members in the Renegade material play somewhat subtle political games, kidnap and magically indoctrinate folks, cajole and convince and give chiminage and successfully interact with Gaian spirits all without killing anyone ( well, openly at least).<br /> <br /> Or are there members of the CoF that are unaffected by Hauglosk that do all the groundwork infiltration stuff without murderising everything in sight and others who do all the obey me or die death frenzy stuff. Kind of like the Legacy BSD ' normal seeming' recruiters vs the masses of physically corrupted Hive-dwellers that are too insane to do much more than kill everything in sight.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I don't mean to be sarcastic but....didn't the Ten Tips mostly talk about this? What do you think they mean to this?<br /> <br /> Hauglosk is the symptom not the cause seems particularly relevant.<br /> <br /> The Cult of Fenris is everything the Garou were taken to the 11 and showing how it can easily go horribly horribly wrong.<br /> <br /> So of course they don't have any problem recruiting Garou since it's going from antihero to villain.<br /> <br /> They're reactionaries to Garou conservatives and those people NEVER run out of followers. Nor do they hesitate to do violence to people that disagree with them or do not fit their idealized image of [insert group]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> 