https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T12:35:47-08:00","id":1529457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1529445#post1529445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about giving Parawolf both middle fingers and actually playing as the Cult of Fenrir?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1529446#post1529446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See what Sambrano said on the previous page, it would basically be like playing nazis. Even if the numbers are filed off, that was the core concept Muammar pushed.</div> </div> </div> </div>At my table I'll play what ever I want and I don't care what anybody at Paradox (or anywhere else for that matter) thinks.<br /> <br /> That said, if I'm just blowing off W5, then I'd just play a werewolf in the Get of Fenris and ignore the new fluff. Though, I have to admit, there is something appealing to me about turning the new material on its head and playing a member of the Cult of Fenris - all other tribes have fallen to apathy and harano, only one group of Garou still have the courage to stand up and fight against the Wyrm - the Cult of Fenris. Something like that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T13:16:04-08:00","id":1529459,"title":"","content":"You can't give corporations the middle finger by buying their products and then using them in was unintended in the privacy of your own home. I'll opt for a language companies tend to understand: not buying their worst-iteration of Werewolf products. There's nothing in W5 I can't play in other games, and I don't have to reward Paradox's shitty behavior by adding to their sales figures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":7},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T13:59:44-08:00","id":1529464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1529459#post1529459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't give corporations the middle finger by buying their products and then using them in was unintended in the privacy of your own home. I'll opt for a language companies tend to understand: not buying their worst-iteration of Werewolf products. There's nothing in W5 I can't play in other games, and I don't have to reward Paradox's shitty behavior by adding to their sales figures.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this is my biggest issue with trying to &quot;save&quot; anything in W5 that still involves the actual gamebook. From its development to its content to its mechanics, it's just rotten to the core. It's not even like V5 where it could act as a decent enough intro to very new players. It offers nothing you can't get much better from just adjusting WtA20th slightly. Its mechanics hate the players and its development was abusive. There's no point. The best thing to do is to not buy it at all.<br /> <br /> You'd have to completely overhaul it into something entirely new and seaprate to make it worthwhile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","user":"gh0st-fox","date":". 01-25-2024, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T14:14:00-08:00","id":1529466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1529459#post1529459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't give corporations the middle finger by buying their products and then using them in was unintended in the privacy of your own home. I'll opt for a language companies tend to understand: not buying their worst-iteration of Werewolf products. There's nothing in W5 I can't play in other games, and I don't have to reward Paradox's shitty behavior by adding to their sales figures.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why you buy a secondhand copy to avoid giving them your money, record yourself playing the game in a way they don't like and tweeting it to them in a very public manner, hehe<br /> <br /> In all seriousness, I'm not paying for any WoD5 books at all. So no worries on my end with that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T15:07:57-08:00","id":1529467,"title":"","content":"I think the next article will be about Subsidiaries in W5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T16:16:01-08:00","id":1529471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gh0st-fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1529464#post1529464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, this is my biggest issue with trying to &quot;save&quot; anything in W5 that still involves the actual gamebook. From its development to its content to its mechanics, it's just rotten to the core. It's not even like V5 where it could act as a decent enough intro to very new players. It offers nothing you can't get much better from just adjusting WtA20th slightly. Its mechanics hate the players and its development was abusive. There's no point. The best thing to do is to not buy it at all.<br /> <br /> You'd have to completely overhaul it into something entirely new and seaprate to make it worthwhile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. With V5 there are certain metaplot elements that I like, and while my group will stick to playing V20, there are portions of V5 that I'll take and drop into my V20 games. I don't see myself wanting to have anything to do with W5, not even taking pieces of it to use in W20 games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T05:44:19-08:00","id":1529700,"title":"","content":"Every other thing I read about the construction of WEREWOLF 5th edition makes it sound as though the World of Darkness stopped being published at White Wolf and started being published by survivors of Black Dog - no, not that one, the Pentex subsidiary - who got sick of being an affectionate self-parody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T09:16:44-08:00","id":1530035,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not sure this will add much to the discussion, but I was reading the old GET OF FENRIS TRIBEBOOK and thought it might be fun to puzzle out what befell the various camps after the Great Unpleasantness suggested by Mr Phipps (A Fenrir version of \u2018Execute Order 66\u2019 as it were).<br /> <br /> Fair warning: having only seen previews of the revised tribebook, this will be based on out-of-date information.<br /> <br /> <br /> THE VALKYRIES OF FREYA - Whether in the classic editions or in 5th edition, the one thing we can reasonably be certain of is that they would NEVER end up with the Black Furies (Albeit in 5th edition that\u2019s more because those Garou inclined to the Furies would have joined that Tribe already*).<br /> <br /> I suspect that this camp is likely to split down the middle, since there\u2019s nothing in their original manifesto to argue for or against their inclusion with the Cult of Fenris (Though one suspects the Camp\u2019s tendency to think for itself - or at least deliberately place itself a little apart from traditional ways of doing things - could potentially make it\u2019s members poor Cultists material).<br /> <br /> *<i>Incidentally, one interesting wrinkle to explore in 5th edition would be the question of which Signature Characters might find their way into very different tribes - since Tribe seems to be a purely spiritual affinity, rather than linked to ancestry or homeland: it\u2019s possible to imagine Evan Heals-the-Past winding up in the neo-Black Furies with Mari Cabrah, for instance (If the key element of his personality was a desire for Justice; an emphasis on Leadership might well see him land with the new style Silver Fangs).</i><br /> <br /> <br /> THE HAND OF TYR - Brutally uncompromising from the start, the Hand\u2019s focus on Justice over Vengeance means that those of their membership who went the way of the Cult would be more regretted than most, not least because the Cult of Fenris\u2019 commitment to the \u2018Cult of the Offensive\u2019 is likely to see these sleuths, judges and executioners dragged into large scale operations at odd with the Hand\u2019s focus on the individual (Though it\u2019s possible members of the Hand may try to carve a niche as assassins, investigators and spies for the Cult).<br /> <br /> Those members of the Hand who refused to join the Cult - who would likely appreciate their attitude, if not always their exacting approach to things - would almost certainly be amongst the most eager to mete out retributive justice on the Cultists (It seems highly likely these survivors would be appreciated by the relentless Galestalkers for their hunting skills and by the Black Furies for their commitment to Justice red in tooth &amp; claw).<br /> <br /> <br /> MJOLNIR\u2019S THUNDER - Quite possibly the most elemental Cult of Fenris members, in that they want the Wyrm dead and don\u2019t really give a d*** about anything else so long as it ends up blasted: on the other hand this makes them completely malice free, so far as humanity is concerned, which is something.<br /> <br /> Still not interested in minimising collateral damage, though: if members of this Camp fail to continue with the Cult of Fenris after the Great Unpleasantness, it\u2019s probably out of loyalty to those of their tribe who were removed from the equation so that the Cult could run everything.<br /> <br /> The real question is whether the \u2018Hammers\u2019 would immediately identify the Cult as Wyrm-tainted or just as another case of politics winning out over the actual Mission (In either case I\u2019d bet the Shadow Lords would be just delighted to acquire defectors, if only as Muscle: whether the defectors would be delighted to be acquired or head over to the Hart Warden instead is an interesting question).<br /> <br /> <br /> THE FANGS OF GARM - \u2018Public Enemy #1\u2019 aka \u2018Priority Targets\u2019 in Cult of Fenris terms, it seems highly likely that a Tribal moot summoned to address the absolute lunacy of leaving the Blood Fist caern deserted for the sake of murdering slightly more Wyrmspawn was the key forum for the \u2018Great Unpleasantness\u2019 (AKA the Massacre of the Scrupulous\u2019).<br /> <br /> If this was indeed the case, then it\u2019s a racing certainty that this purge of those Fenrir with the strongest ties to other tribes is a key reason the Cult of Fenris appears on the enemies list in the fifth edition Corebook,<br /> <br /> If any survivors made it through the massacre (and the Get are almost as tough as they try to be, so someight Well have) it seems likely they would have a strong chance of making their way into another tribe (and I\u2019d bet money that a strong minority of the multi-tribe sept now holding the Blood Fist caern would have been Fangs of Garm to start with - assuming that these would have been negotiating with those packs from other tribes garrisoning the caern whilst the Fenrir worked to settle internal controversies at a more private forum).<br /> <br /> <br /> THE GLORIOUS FIST OF WOTAN - Almost certainly made up a solid majority of the original Cult and would be just delighted to purge those who didn\u2019t see things their way from the former tribe, probably to the point of being the Driving Force behind the \u2018Great Unpleasantness\u2019.<br /> <br /> Presumably entirely happy as they work and plan to teach Humanity some bloody lessons on a scale their former tribe mates would have been deeply reluctant to contemplate (Mighty also be kept working to maintain their ascendancy over the Cult and expand the Cult by snapping up the most extremist elements from across what\u2019s left of the Garou Nation).<br /> <br /> <br /> THE SWORDS OF HEIMDALL - were very, very dead before the Great Unpleasantness and, since they didn\u2019t get graves to start with, can\u2019t crawl out of them.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately the Cult of Fenris are busily enabling their ideological bedfellows, because when the Tribes of the Garou Nation aren\u2019t taking your call, mortals with an unhealthy attitude towards old myths of Northern Europe and White Racial Supremacy will still answer the dog-whistle.<br /> <br /> At least when you\u2019re a Ragnarok Cult made up of Big Bad Wolves looking for footsoldiers (AKA \u2018cannon fodder\u2019).<br /> <br /> <br /> YMIR\u2019S SWEAT - I tend to operate on the assumption that 5th edition tribes are more \u2018religions\u2019 than nationalities, with the latter role being handled by septs.<br /> <br /> One therefore assumes that Ymir\u2019s Sweat (I\u2019ve never been certain if that should have been an actual camp or more of a running joke/folk legend even in the Classic editions) is a sept active somewhere in the Maritime Provinces of Canada - and was probably split down the middle, much like the majority of Fenris Wolf\u2019s children.<br /> <br /> <br /> LOKI\u2019S SMILE - Whether they actually existed as Fenrir of uncommonly devious ambition in the classic editions (Or were, in fact, an insurgency within one of the most aggressively strong tribes sponsored by the Shadow Lords) it\u2019s not hard to believe that Loki\u2019s Smile would work perfectly as a group the Cult of Fenris loudly deny, but which plays some influential covert role within the Cult.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s horribly easy to imagine the \u2018Smilers with a Knife\u2019 playing a key role in making the Great Unpleasantness possible - if only because a Cult is, on the whole, easier to manipulate than a nation (Though the vicious single-mindedness of Hauglosk-ridden Garou means it\u2019s still dangerous to assume they\u2019ll rocket off in the direction you want them to go).<br /> <br /> Whether this was a result of the \u2018Smilers\u2019 genuinely sharing the Cult\u2019s love of a Glorious Death or was more grounded in a desire to make sure that if these fools were going to devote themselves to suicide missions, it was better to steer them towards useful deaths is an interesting question.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s possible that those who preferred to seek greener pastures elsewhere might have fallen in with the Shadow Lords with whom they often seem to share a few flourishes, but it\u2019s equally (possibly more likely) they would seek out Tribes where trading on their particular skills would not be like selling a refrigerator to a man who lives in an igloo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T09:17:43-08:00","id":1530036,"title":"","content":"^^ Thank Goodness, it posted! ^^<br /> <br /> Truly, the Weaver is a powerful, powerful foe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T04:49:03-08:00","id":1530365,"title":"","content":"It occurred to me that it might be interesting to puzzle out what the Litany, as taught to the Cult of Fenris may look like: I\u2019m assuming that they would happily discard those elements which struck them as inconvenient (and generally interpret whatever was left to suit themselves).<br /> <br /> - COMBAT THE WYRM WHEREVER IT DWELLS AND WHEREVER IT THRIVES<br /> <br /> - ACCEPT AN HONOURABLE SURRENDER<br /> <br /> - RESPECT THOSE OF LOWER STATION<br /> <br /> - THE FIRST SHARE OF THE KILL FOR THE GREATEST IN STATION<br /> <br /> - EAT NOT THE FLESH OF HUMANS<br /> <br /> - THE VEIL SHALL NOT BE LIFTED<br /> <br /> - DO NOT OBLIGE THE PEOPLE TO TEND YOUR SICKNESS<br /> <br /> - THE LEADER MAY NOT BE CHALLENGED DURING WARTIME<br /> <br /> - TAKE NO ACTION THAT CAUSES A CAERN TO BE VIOLATED<br /> <br /> (I\u2019m also fairly convinced that \u2018GAROU SHALL NOT MATE WITH GAROU\u2019 was seriously proposed - a majority of the Cult of Fenris wants it\u2019s members focussed on the Apocalypse War and an honourable death, not wasting time making children that cannot be expected to see adulthood*).<br /> <br /> <i>*After all, to their way of thinking The End may come at any time.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28339,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","user":"Atticus Cleanclaw","date":".  Thumb slipped, post previously incomplete. 02-09-2024, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T04:58:25-08:00","id":1530367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1530365#post1530365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It occurred to me that it might be interesting to puzzle out what the Litany, as taught to the Cult of Fenris may look like: I\u2019m assuming that they would</div> </div> </div> </div>A clever interpretation might insert some of the old rules like Garou breeding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T05:05:41-08:00","id":1530368,"title":"","content":"Depicting the Cult as only willing to accept recreational <i>hem-hem</i> and not actual family-building would be an excellent way to hint at something rather worse than \u2018No Garou Nation bull**** here\u2019.<br /> <br /> The key element to capturing the Cult\u2019s villainy is to evoke not only a brutally uncompromising attitude to enemies, but a callously dismissive attitude to the very notion that one can enjoy a somewhat settled family life even if the Cause and the Curse mean you can\u2019t really live a peaceful existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T05:11:15-08:00","id":1530370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1530365#post1530365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I\u2019m also fairly convinced that \u2018GAROU SHALL NOT MATE WITH GAROU\u2019 was seriously proposed - a majority of the Cult of Fenris wants it\u2019s members focussed on the Apocalypse War and an honourable death, not wasting time making children that cannot be expected to see adulthood*).[/I]</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're bringing back the Crinos-born and that element of the lore, it does bear keeping in mind that one of them can fight from infancy and be a fully fledged member of society within 3-6 years of their birth. They seem like quite a good investment for the Cult (and why they were a major thing for the BSD's in past versions)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T05:28:41-08:00","id":1530371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1530365#post1530365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurred to me that it might be interesting to puzzle out what the Litany, as taught to the Cult of Fenris may look like: I\u2019m assuming that they would happily discard those elements which struck them as inconvenient (and generally interpret whatever was left to suit themselves).<br /> <br /> - COMBAT THE WYRM WHEREVER IT DWELLS AND WHEREVER IT THRIVES<br /> <br /> - ACCEPT AN HONOURABLE SURRENDER<br /> <br /> - RESPECT THOSE OF LOWER STATION<br /> <br /> - THE FIRST SHARE OF THE KILL FOR THE GREATEST IN STATION<br /> <br /> - EAT NOT THE FLESH OF HUMANS<br /> <br /> - THE VEIL SHALL NOT BE LIFTED<br /> <br /> - DO NOT OBLIGE THE PEOPLE TO TEND YOUR SICKNESS<br /> <br /> - THE LEADER MAY NOT BE CHALLENGED DURING WARTIME<br /> <br /> - TAKE NO ACTION THAT CAUSES A CAERN TO BE VIOLATED<br /> <br /> (I\u2019m also fairly convinced that \u2018GAROU SHALL NOT MATE WITH GAROU\u2019 was seriously proposed - a majority of the Cult of Fenris wants it\u2019s members focussed on the Apocalypse War and an honourable death, not wasting time making children that cannot be expected to see adulthood*).<br /> <br /> <i>*After all, to their way of thinking The End may come at any time.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I think one way to emphasize the callous nature of the Cult would be to remove the last two, the one about honorable surrender and respect for those of lower station. Protecting caerns is irrelevant because the world is doomed, the only thing that matters is combating the Wyrm. And the challenge-thing gets removed because the Cult has a far more sadistic view of how it operates as an organization. So the only mantra for the organization is &quot;might makes right&quot;. There's no real camaraderie anymore, just the brutality that equally exists in how the Cult treats their enemies as well as in how they treat each other.<br /> <br /> And I think bringing back Crinos-born could work if it's coupled with the old breeding-lore. You can use that to build up a contrast between the other Garou and the Cult. Whereas the other Garou have started caring less and less about Crinos-born being this stigmatized group of people and more and more Septs are just fine with accepting them as full-fledged members on equal footing, the Cult on the other hand has gone in the opposite direction. They are of the fanatical belief that the correct number of Crinos-born in the Garou-Nation should be zero. And so they have this merciless kill-on-sight policy for Crinos-born. The logic being there's something fundamentally wrong with Crinos-born in the mind of the Cult and it's part of their zealous faith to just assume that if there are simply no Crinos-born in the Garou-Nation everything will be just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T05:33:35-08:00","id":1530373,"title":"","content":"That wasn\u2019t actually my intent - my notion was more grounded in the idea that the Cult doesn\u2019t want it\u2019s female warriors pregnant when they could be fighting and is deliberately cultivating a \u2018Love them and leave them\u2019 attitude to romantic relationships in the interests of ensuring that a Fenrisian\u2019s<br /> loyalty is to the Cult and to the Last Battle, not any loved ones.<br /> <br /> This is somewhat harder if their loved ones are fighting right beside them (Actually, the likely tendency of 5th edition Garou to form packs grounded on such romantic relationships is an interesting new wrinkle, though I suspect the damage two lovers with Rage can potentially do to EVERYONE is a sound argument in favour of an historic taboo against getting too tangled up with a fellow werewolf, even amongst the less fanatic elements of the Garou Nation*).<br /> <br /> While the rarity of First Change means that we\u2019re unlikely to see who packs built on a nuclear family, it is possible that some Garou packs mirror their plain wolf counterparts, with mother and father wolf running alongside a mix of born and adopted children (I suspect that the Red Talons and Silver Fangs, possibly even the Galestalkers and Hart Wardens would be especially keen on this way of doing things.<br /> <br /> *<i>Though if this was ever a formal part of the Litany then it would have been discarded - and probably discarded long since.<br /> <br /> <br /> </i>Incidentally<i>, </i>with regard to the classic editions of WEREWOLF, I\u2019ve seen and very agree with the suggestion that the Black Spiral Dancer\u2019s mass breeding of \u2018Metis\u2019 gives them a short-term advantage only at a serious long-term cost: if nothing else, reducing female Black Spiral Dancers to breeding stock is likely to have a profoundly toxic impact on the status of women in their society (Especially when breeding a child of Rage is very, very dangerous for any pregnant Garou).<br /> <br /> Given the ubiquitous use of inhuman wave tactics and general tendency to spend lives without care associated with the BSDs, in an timeline where the Apocalypse does NOT occur on schedule the Tribe of the Fallen will almost certainly be facing a serious demographic crisis.<br /> <br /> Honestly, it\u2019s a pity that 5th Edition doesn\u2019t really allow us to play with these ideas, since it\u2019s more low-key \u2019Cold War\u2019 feel makes it a natural stage on which to explore the consequences of the Apocalypse War going hot \u2026 only to cool off before the world can boil away.<br /> <br /> Having said that the BY NIGHT studios version of WEREWOLF offers a similar opportunity and does retain the old Homid/Too Pure/Lupus breed paradigm.<br /> <br /> There have to be some advantages to having a multiverse after all, eh?\ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T05:45:37-08:00","id":1530375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1530371#post1530371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think one way to emphasize the callous nature of the Cult would be to remove the last two, the one about honorable surrender and respect for those of lower station. Protecting caerns is irrelevant because the world is doomed, the only thing that matters is combating the Wyrm. And the challenge-thing gets removed because the Cult has a far more sadistic view of how it operates as an organization. So the only mantra for the organization is &quot;might makes right&quot;. There's no real camaraderie anymore, just the brutality that equally exists in how the Cult treats their enemies as well as in how they treat each other.</div> </div> </div> </div> That\u2019s a fair point (Doubtless some elements within the Cult absolutely would advocate for such changes and would certainly practice such an attitude): my own approach was to presume that there\u2019s a strong element in the Cult (Especially<br /> prominent in leadership positions) which regards themselves as the Vanguard of Garou society, rather than completely cut off from the Nation - and is also eager to avoid Cult<br /> members killing other Fenrisians, hence support for an Honourable Surrender.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a way of encouraging an \u2018Us against the World\u2019 atttiude rather than breeding a war of All against All (One should also note that I take it as an article of faith that, even when the world is ending, Garou veneration for caerns remains bone-deep even amongst a majority of the Fenrisians, however large or small that minority: it\u2019s not really practical for them to hold caerns, given the challenges posed by Hauglosk, but they will die fighting to defend them \u2026 unless local leadership falls to one lost to the Killing Grief).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T09:49:26-08:00","id":1530388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1530365#post1530365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurred to me that it might be interesting to puzzle out what the Litany, as taught to the Cult of Fenris may look like: I\u2019m assuming that they would happily discard those elements which struck them as inconvenient (and generally interpret whatever was left to suit themselves).<br /> <br /> - COMBAT THE WYRM WHEREVER IT DWELLS AND WHEREVER IT THRIVES<br /> <br /> - ACCEPT AN HONOURABLE SURRENDER<br /> <br /> - RESPECT THOSE OF LOWER STATION<br /> <br /> - THE FIRST SHARE OF THE KILL FOR THE GREATEST IN STATION<br /> <br /> - EAT NOT THE FLESH OF HUMANS<br /> <br /> - THE VEIL SHALL NOT BE LIFTED<br /> <br /> - DO NOT OBLIGE THE PEOPLE TO TEND YOUR SICKNESS<br /> <br /> - THE LEADER MAY NOT BE CHALLENGED DURING WARTIME<br /> <br /> - TAKE NO ACTION THAT CAUSES A CAERN TO BE VIOLATED<br /> <br /> (I\u2019m also fairly convinced that \u2018GAROU SHALL NOT MATE WITH GAROU\u2019 was seriously proposed - a majority of the Cult of Fenris wants it\u2019s members focussed on the Apocalypse War and an honourable death, not wasting time making children that cannot be expected to see adulthood*).<br /> <br /> <i>*After all, to their way of thinking The End may come at any time.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Lights, camera, W5 mode on and action!<br /> <br /> <br /> - COMBAT THE WYRM WHEREVER IT DWELLS AND WHEREVER IT THRIVES<br /> <br /> &quot;This first one is straight to the point as well as being stupidly obvious, the Wyrm is the enemy and it is because of her that things are as they are, regardless of what others say, and we are the warriors of Gaia and our duty consists of this, to eliminate the Wyrm wherever it is and not just it, but anyone who serves it's purposes, whether he is a creature of the Wyrm, a human, or even another Garou, whether they are aware of it or not. Some may find this rule too harsh and extreme, but this is a war and there is no &quot;extreme&quot; attitude in a war, all that matters is winning, especially when it comes to a just cause like ours and if you still have any doubts, just look at the state we are in now, this shithole that the world has become is because of those who believed we were being too violent, well if they weren't so worried about bullshit and started killing more we wouldn't be in as much shit as we are now.&quot;<br /> <br /> - ACCEPT AN HONOURABLE SURRENDER<br /> <br /> &quot;This one is simple, even if some bootlickers like to complicate it more than necessary. We Garou are creatures prone to letting ourselves be carried away by our emotions, I believe you already know that at this point, naturally this makes us have many conflicts between ourselves for various reasons, but understand that this isn't necessarily bad, it keeps us sharp and always ready for combat, however we also are a species at risk, there are not enough Garou in the world and to be honest I don't know if one day our species will recover, so whenever we can we must preserve our kind, so when you and your pack brother fight, remember to accept his surrender and don't be ashamed to surrender if you lose, you will serve better off staying alive. Now, and it's unfortunate that I need to make this clear, this rule is for Garous only, don't even think about accepting the surrender of a servant of the Wyrm, if you do it's likely you won't live long enough to regret it, and even if you do, believe me, I will guarantee you that you will never think about doing it a second time.\u201d<br /> <br /> - RESPECT THOSE OF LOWER STATION<br /> <br /> &quot;That's easy, it's a rule to remind an alpha that he is nothing without his pack, Garous are creatures that live and act in groups and for a leader the worst thing that can happen is someone stabbing him in the back, I'm not saying to spoil them, an alpha must know when to be tough so his pack doesn't go soft, but if he's too tough or doesn't show himself worthy, disaster could end up happening, that's what this rule is about. As for humans and the other tribes, they may have deserved our respect once, but today they have made too many mistakes to let it go, we can't just pretend to forget what they did, if they want any respect, first they must recognize their place in Gaia's grand plan or die like the ignorant fools they are.&quot;<br /> <br /> - THE FIRST SHARE OF THE KILL FOR THE GREATEST IN STATION<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't know why this rule is there. Depending on who you ask, it refers to prioritizing your resources by giving them to the strongest Garou, but if he is the strongest he will naturally get those resources. My guess is that this rule was made, so that the greedy leaders would maintain their corrupt control and take away what was rightful from the true Garou.&quot;<br /> <br /> - EAT NOT THE FLESH OF HUMANS<br /> <br /> &quot;This rule is there for two good reasons. The first is that you shouldn't kill humans unnecessarily, do not hesitate to do so if necessary, but as I already said, we Garou are a dying species and whether we like it or not we still need humans, because We don't know if any of them could be potential Garou, so avoid killing them for any reason. The second reason and this is much more important, human flesh is addictive, I've seen honorable Garou become mangy creatures after consuming some human flesh, even if without knowing it, before you arrived I knew a Garou who ate human flesh once, and he would often lose focus during battle, and disappear during the night and come back with his fur soaked in blood, he tried to stop, but the abstinence was so great that he ate his own fingers, without much to do we put an end to his suffering, it's a sad fate.&quot;<br /> <br /> - THE VEIL SHALL NOT BE LIFTED<br /> <br /> &quot;In other words, don't reveal yourself to humans, we are stronger and faster than them, but they surpass us in numbers and weapons, so it's better not to give them a reason to start hunting us. I know this can It may seem like cowardice, but we have a war to win and we only have to lose by starting unnecessary battles.&quot;<br /> <br /> - DO NOT OBLIGE THE PEOPLE TO TEND YOUR SICKNESS<br /> <br /> &quot;A tough and sometimes sad law, but it needs to be followed, this is a war and as you know our resources are limited, so we can't use them on those who can no longer fight, we don't like making this decision, but it is necessary, also no son of Fenrir would be content to die of old age or as a dead weight, we die on the battlefield and will accept nothing less.&quot;<br /> <br /> - THE LEADER MAY NOT BE CHALLENGED DURING WARTIME<br /> <br /> &quot;A little confusing since we are always at war. What it really means is that during a battle you don't question your leader, internal fights will only make you lose the battle and most likely your life. Now other than in these cases, there is nothing wrong in challenge your leader when all your enemies are down, an alpha needs to be constantly challenged to stay strong otherwise he will only become slow and weak and this will lead to the death of the pack, this is what happened with most other tribes, their elders refused to lose their positions and give the opportunity to a more trustworthy Garou, making excuses to refuse challenge, so the leader not only remained, but became complacent, that's not a Garou, just a filthy pig dressed as a wolf and a pack that do nothing deserve a leader like that&quot;<br /> <br /> - TAKE NO ACTION THAT CAUSES A CAERN TO BE VIOLATED<br /> <br /> &quot;Also obvious, but also the most sacred rule, the Caerns are vital to our species and must be protected tooth and nail and if anyone puts it at risk in any way the punishment must be only one, DEATH. We do what we can to defend our Caerns, the other Tribes claim to do the same, but don't be fooled, they are not doing enough, they can say what they want, but I listen to the stories and I know how to separate the truth from the lies. Have you ever heard about that Caern in New York? The one on top of a building? The damned Glass Walkers got help from some &quot;trusted&quot; relatives to protect the place, they even got military equipment, but everything collapsed when the hunters entered through the frontdoor and put a silver bullet in everyone's head and all they had to do was bribe one of these &quot;trusted&quot; relatives. I could sit here for hours and tell you all the stories I've heard, but they all end the same way, Caerns being brought down because someone couldn't keep his mouth shut and do his dawn job. Caerns, must be protected and only entrusted to Garous.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T16:14:52-08:00","id":1530408,"title":"","content":"Psicose, if I had a hat - wait a minute, I borrowed my name from WEREWOLF: THE WILD WEST, clearly my Internet Avatar has an absolutely splendid chapeau.<br /> <br /> I therefore doff my hat to you for putting together such a delightfully brutal (Though not wholly brutish) ramble through the mind of a fairly typical Fenrisian.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, my presumption is that the parts of this \u2018pruned\u2019 version of The Litany which mention \u2018the greatest in station\u2019 and \u2018the leader\u2019 are a subtle way of stressing that there IS a hierarchy (and that wise Fenrisians respect the fact), partly to avoid compete anarchy and just possibly as a means of letting outsiders know that if you want to deal with the Cult of Fenris you start at the top.<br /> <br /> The mention of \u2018during wartime\u2019 is meant to emphasise that the Cult of Fenris are soldiers at war, not hooligans on a spree (Also that when the boss puts his foot down, you JUMP).<br /> <br /> It\u2019s vaguely possible that some outsiders might interpret this to mean that there\u2019s at least a small possibility the Cult may not always be at War - these outsiders are most kindly described as \u2018optimists\u2019.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T17:03:11-08:00","id":1530412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1530388#post1530388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lights, camera, W5 mode on and ac