ter consuming some human flesh, even if without knowing it, before you arrived I knew a Garou who ate human flesh once, and he would often lose focus during battle, and disappear during the night and come back with his fur soaked in blood, he tried to stop, but the abstinence was so great that he ate his own fingers, without much to do we put an end to his suffering, it's a sad fate.&quot;<br /> <br /> - THE VEIL SHALL NOT BE LIFTED<br /> <br /> &quot;In other words, don't reveal yourself to humans, we are stronger and faster than them, but they surpass us in numbers and weapons, so it's better not to give them a reason to start hunting us. I know this can It may seem like cowardice, but we have a war to win and we only have to lose by starting unnecessary battles.&quot;<br /> <br /> - DO NOT OBLIGE THE PEOPLE TO TEND YOUR SICKNESS<br /> <br /> &quot;A tough and sometimes sad law, but it needs to be followed, this is a war and as you know our resources are limited, so we can't use them on those who can no longer fight, we don't like making this decision, but it is necessary, also no son of Fenrir would be content to die of old age or as a dead weight, we die on the battlefield and will accept nothing less.&quot;<br /> <br /> - THE LEADER MAY NOT BE CHALLENGED DURING WARTIME<br /> <br /> &quot;A little confusing since we are always at war. What it really means is that during a battle you don't question your leader, internal fights will only make you lose the battle and most likely your life. Now other than in these cases, there is nothing wrong in challenge your leader when all your enemies are down, an alpha needs to be constantly challenged to stay strong otherwise he will only become slow and weak and this will lead to the death of the pack, this is what happened with most other tribes, their elders refused to lose their positions and give the opportunity to a more trustworthy Garou, making excuses to refuse challenge, so the leader not only remained, but became complacent, that's not a Garou, just a filthy pig dressed as a wolf and a pack that do nothing deserve a leader like that&quot;<br /> <br /> - TAKE NO ACTION THAT CAUSES A CAERN TO BE VIOLATED<br /> <br /> &quot;Also obvious, but also the most sacred rule, the Caerns are vital to our species and must be protected tooth and nail and if anyone puts it at risk in any way the punishment must be only one, DEATH. We do what we can to defend our Caerns, the other Tribes claim to do the same, but don't be fooled, they are not doing enough, they can say what they want, but I listen to the stories and I know how to separate the truth from the lies. Have you ever heard about that Caern in New York? The one on top of a building? The damned Glass Walkers got help from some &quot;trusted&quot; relatives to protect the place, they even got military equipment, but everything collapsed when the hunters entered through the frontdoor and put a silver bullet in everyone's head and all they had to do was bribe one of these &quot;trusted&quot; relatives. I could sit here for hours and tell you all the stories I've heard, but they all end the same way, Caerns being brought down because someone couldn't keep his mouth shut and do his dawn job. Caerns, must be protected and only entrusted to Garous.</div> </div> </div> </div>That last one seems to be wrong based on info so far as we have 2 canon depictions of Cultists abandoning Caerns and one of them destroying a Caern.<br /> <br /> And the Fenrir are also depicted as having ' in the know' human foot soldiers unlike the rest of the W5 ' Nation'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 02-09-2024, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T02:32:55-08:00","id":1530426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1530375#post1530375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s a fair point (Doubtless some elements within the Cult absolutely would advocate for such changes and would certainly practice such an attitude): my own approach was to presume that there\u2019s a strong element in the Cult (Especially<br /> prominent in leadership positions) which regards themselves as the Vanguard of Garou society, rather than completely cut off from the Nation - and is also eager to avoid Cult<br /> members killing other Fenrisians, hence support for an Honourable Surrender.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a way of encouraging an \u2018Us against the World\u2019 atttiude rather than breeding a war of All against All (One should also note that I take it as an article of faith that, even when the world is ending, Garou veneration for caerns remains bone-deep even amongst a majority of the Fenrisians, however large or small that minority: it\u2019s not really practical for them to hold caerns, given the challenges posed by Hauglosk, but they will die fighting to defend them \u2026 unless local leadership falls to one lost to the Killing Grief).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think, an important part that you point out there is that you have to decide to what degree you portray them as Garou-extremists (they're still the same warriors fighting for a cause but now with extremist and fundamentalist tendencies) or whether you focus on the &quot;Cult&quot;-part in the name and instead make it about zealous religiosity, obedience and millenarian beliefs. If you try to link it more to the Get of Fenris Tribe and what they were about, I think what you describe works better. The only thing that makes me want to focus on the &quot;Cult&quot;-part more is that I'm looking for a way to integrate the part of the Deepest of Wounds adventure with the torture/brainwashing-scene. After all, the description of the Fenrir's beliefs and organization becomes very different once you add the concept of magical brainwashing as a recruitment-tool, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T03:06:14-08:00","id":1530428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1530426#post1530426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I think, an important part that you point out there is that you have to decide to what degree you portray them as Garou-extremists (they're still the same warriors fighting for a cause but now with extremist and fundamentalist tendencies) or whether you focus on the &quot;Cult&quot;-part in the name and instead make it about zealous religiosity, obedience and millenarian beliefs. If you try to link it more to the Get of Fenris Tribe and what they were about, I think what you describe works better. The only thing that makes me want to focus on the &quot;Cult&quot;-part more is that I'm looking for a way to integrate the part of the Deepest of Wounds adventure with the torture/brainwashing-scene. After all, the description of the Fenrir's beliefs and organization becomes very different once you add the concept of magical brainwashing as a recruitment-tool, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a perfectly valid way to portray the Cult is, &quot;They're Garou who are acting the same way as always but are ALSO 20% worse and fighting other Garou for resources, ideological purity, and just because they're in a bad mood.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which means the greatest sin of the Cult is they're just not helping things when every hand needs to be on deck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T08:38:52-08:00","id":1530451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1530428#post1530428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think a perfectly valid way to portray the Cult is, &quot;They're Garou who are acting the same way as always but are ALSO 20% worse and fighting other Garou for resources, ideological purity, and just because they're in a bad mood.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which means the greatest sin of the Cult is they're just not helping things when every hand needs to be on deck.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of doubt this is the presentation that we'll be getting, given that the other tribes don't exactly put many hands on deck as far as anyone knows, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T11:13:55-08:00","id":1530461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1530451#post1530451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I kind of doubt this is the presentation that we'll be getting, given that the other tribes don't exactly put many hands on deck as far as anyone knows, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't they?<br /> <br /> I mean, it was badly presented, but everything we've seen in spin-off media (Earthblood, Heart of the Forest, and the sample adventures) all indicates the Garou are all doing the fight the Wyrm thing still.<br /> <br /> They also only get Reknown for fighting the Wyrm and doing the same things they always did.<br /> <br /> The book just is very judgy about ir.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T11:29:47-08:00","id":1530463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1530461#post1530461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aren't they?<br /> <br /> I mean, it was badly presented, but everything we've seen in spin-off media (Earthblood, Heart of the Forest, and the sample adventures) all indicates the Garou are all doing the fight the Wyrm thing still.<br /> <br /> They also only get Reknown for fighting the Wyrm and doing the same things they always did.<br /> <br /> The book just is very judgy about ir.</div> </div> </div> </div>The official website makes clear that Earthblood and Heart of the Forest aren't part of the W5-canon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . Those games aren't indicators of how the Cult of Fenris works in W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T13:38:43-08:00","id":1530474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1530463#post1530463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The official website makes clear that Earthblood and Heart of the Forest aren't part of the W5-canon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . Those games aren't indicators of how the Cult of Fenris works in W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean....no, it doesn't.<br /> <br /> It says <b>parts of them</b> aren't canon. They're listed as absolutely part of the canon as a whole, though.<br /> <br /> I presume the parts are the fact that Cahill is called a Fianna and other forbidden names show up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T13:56:02-08:00","id":1530478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1530474#post1530474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean....no, it doesn't.<br /> <br /> It says <b>parts of them</b> aren't canon. They're listed as absolutely part of the canon as a whole, though.<br /> <br /> I presume the parts are the fact that Cahill is called a Fianna and other forbidden names show up.</div> </div> </div> </div>sigh<br /> <br /> Come on... What you said makes zero sense. &quot;Parts of this aren't canon&quot; and &quot;This is absolutely part of the canon as a whole&quot; <i>can't</i> be true at the same time. That's just gibberish.<br /> <br /> You know, though, when &quot;parts of this aren't [ W5 ] canon&quot; and &quot;This is absolutely part of the canon as a whole&quot; are a good description...? In fan-fiction. Or, there's another big one that now fits that description: The legacy-editions of WtA. The W5 corebook famously starts with the line &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot; to make clear that it has drawn a line in the sand. And when that line was drawn, Heart of the Forest and Earthblood didn't make the cut. That's the point of the description on the official website.<br /> <br /> But as far as the official W5 canon is concerned, Heart of the Forest and Earthblood are <i>irrelevant</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T15:02:15-08:00","id":1530486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1530474#post1530474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean....no, it doesn't.<br /> <br /> It says <b>parts of them</b> aren't canon. They're listed as absolutely part of the canon as a whole, though.<br /> <br /> I presume the parts are the fact that Cahill is called a Fianna and other forbidden names show up.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's kind of obvious, but as we're not sure which parts are canonical or not, we can't use it as a reference, as far as we know, this game could have been designed in W20 and without knowing what the final form of W5 would be like and they gave it a warning because if they were to use something from the plot or create a sequel that would explain the inaccuracies. That said, this part may also have been changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T15:06:01-08:00","id":1530487,"title":"","content":"I mean, the thing is that it's listed on the official canon page with an asterisk.<br /> <br /> Which is different from being decanonized.<br /> <br /> I think it's worth noting is all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T15:10:42-08:00","id":1530489,"title":"","content":"sigh<br /> <br /> I think it's worth noting that the official website makes it absolutely clear how we should look at these two games: <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"1217\" height=\"813\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/TP9pPnY.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/TP9pPnY.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/TP9pPnY.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> The presentation makes it quite obvious that Heart of the Forest and Earthblood are in a separate category from W5. <b>The W5 corebook has nothing to do with these two games.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T15:23:43-08:00","id":1530491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1530489#post1530489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">sigh<br /> <br /> I think it's worth noting that the official website makes it absolutely clear how we should look at these two games: <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"1217\" height=\"813\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/TP9pPnY.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/TP9pPnY.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/TP9pPnY.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> The presentation makes it quite obvious that Heart of the Forest and Earthblood are in a separate category from W5. <b>The W5 corebook has nothing to do with these two games.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it says, &quot;Some Elements may differ from the fifth Edition setting.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, that logic would mean that Coteries of New York and LA By Night aren't canon to V:TM which they absolutely are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T15:29:33-08:00","id":1530494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1530491#post1530491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, it says, &quot;Some Elements may differ from the fifth Edition setting.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, that logic would mean that Coteries of New York and LA By Night aren't canon to V:TM which they absolutely are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it says &quot;some elements&quot; because they aren't compliant with W5 canon which is why it's also in the categoy of &quot;Released before 5th edition corebook&quot;. And that includes the portrayal of the Fenrir. Also, I'm just presenting you with the fact that officially Heart of the Forest and Earthblood aren't canon according to the official website. You're not arguing with me, you just don't want to accept what is officially canon...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T15:32:14-08:00","id":1530495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1530487#post1530487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the thing is that it's listed on the official canon page with an asterisk.<br /> <br /> Which is different from being decanonized.<br /> <br /> I think it's worth noting is all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying it's not canon just that we don't know what elements remained. You could, for example, say that Cahill wasn't fighting for Gaia, but that he was just protecting the pack's territory, this would change a detail of the story, but the macro remains the same and without clashing with W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T09:57:19-08:00","id":1530560,"title":"","content":"&quot;Some X may differ from $THING&quot; is well-known sanitized corporate speak for &quot;this shit doesn't sync up and we ignored continuity&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T12:40:41-08:00","id":1530575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1530560#post1530560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Some X may differ from $THING&quot; is well-known sanitized corporate speak for &quot;this shit doesn't sync up and we ignored continuity&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet it is still listed as part of the continuity of Fifth Edition as seen here. It is still being sold as a product.<br /> <br /> They could also state that spin off material is not canon at all like they do with Star Trek but they don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T13:02:49-08:00","id":1530580,"title":"","content":"I provided a screenshot that shows that Heart of the Forest and Earthblood are very distinctly listed as <i>not </i>being part of the continuity. Saying otherwise would be an incontrovertible lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T15:26:41-08:00","id":1530590,"title":"","content":"Yes, you did and I just explained how it absolutely does not say what you think it does.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"785\" height=\"450\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/6C6O31j.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/6C6O31j.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/6C6O31j.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Which is getting the matter distracted from as I'm saying that I think <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/BroadStrokes\" target=\"_blank\">Broad Strokes Canon</a> applies. Which is to say if that the entirety of the two games were non-canon, then they wouldn't list them or would say they were entirely non-canon. instead, they seem to be saying that elements of the books are contradictory to later changes made in the core book but that doesn't invalidate the entirety of the work. There's still going to be canonically a Maia the Polish American Garou Kin and a Cahill. The thing that changes about is that, obviously, Cahill is a Heartwarden rather than a member of the Fianna tribe.<br /> <br /> This isn't me attempting to dismiss your point, though. I referred to those two games as an attempt to illustrate that I don't think the Garou Nation isn't a game about sitting around the caern feeling sad now. To use different examples of what the Garou are up to, let's start with CRIMSON THAW (also on the list) which is a bunch of Garou fighting to retake a caern from the Kindred. It is something I recommend because of the black comedy element that the Kindred have NO IDEA what the fuck the Garou are so pissed off about. But it does result in the death of a Camarilla Justicar, which is a pretty impressive accomplishment for any pack (circumstances be different).<br /> <br /> The Renown system is even more tied to fighting the Wyrm than before as well as achieving Gifts. Bluntly, Garou cannot progress on their own or make deals unless they have done the dirty work of killing Wyrmspawn and achieving rank via the old system. We also have &quot;No Matter How Small&quot; which is all about tracking down a Formori serial killer and putting him down for no other reason than he's a Formori corrupted by the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> No offense is intended and I just wanted to share my view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-11-2024, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude21","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T15:46:33-08:00","id":1530591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1530590#post1530590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, you did and I just explained how it absolutely does not say what you think it does.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"785\" height=\"450\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/6C6O31j.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/6C6O31j.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/6C6O31j.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> But if it helps then try CRIMSON THAW which is also listed and has the Garou fight a bunch of vampires and talk about how they're going to destroy the Wyrm and debate the best way to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it says &quot;some elements&quot;... because it's not part of the W5-continuity! That's what that means! Like I said before: &quot;Parts of this aren't canon&quot; and &quot;the whole of this is canon&quot; can't be true at the same time. That's just nonsense.<br /> <br /> But you know what else fits that description...?! Every edition of WtA before this one! The point of W5 is &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;! That's why the official website is making a point of separating W5 from Heart of the Forest and Earthblood (which were released before the official W5 corebook was released)! The point of the description of the official website is that just like all previous lore/editions of WtA, the two games, Heart of the Forest and Earthblood (because they were released before they settled on the version that we got with the official W5 corebook release) are supposed to be seen as <i>separate</i>. The point of &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot; in the W5-corebook is that it's a demarcation to mark a line in the sand between what W5 is/will be and what came before that as a separate thing. Earthblood and Heart of the Forest are part of the &quot;separate thing&quot;. That's why the official website makes clear that those two games deviate from the official W5 canon and were released before the W5 corebook came out. The official website wants people to understand that those two games and W5 are two <i>separate </i>things. The same as previous editions of WtA. That's the goal of this presentation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T15:48:03-08:00","id":1530592,"title":"","content":"I edited my post above to explain my opinion.<br /> <br /> But brass tacks: Maia and Cahill are absolutely still canon but it's not my point. My point is about what Garou are still up to.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have the brand manager's Twitter?<br /> <br /> So we can ask them?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T16:09:46-08:00","id":1530593,"title":"","content":"Oh come on... now you're just shifting the goal-posts... &quot;Broad strokes canon&quot;... seriously?! Now?! Now you want to shift to the reasonable position?! If you had argued that from the start we wouldn't be here!<br /> <br /> Of course, there is a link between Earthblood, Heart of the Forest and the W5-release we got but calling Earthblood and Heart of the Forest &quot;canon&quot; is simply inaccurate. Additionally, nobody of us are mind-readers who know what the writers of the current W5 want to do with the game. Especially because W5 launched with this &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;-premise. The premise of current W5 isn't beholden to what came before (and that includes the two games) so it would be wrong to just assume that those two games show us what W5 will be like. Nobody got tortured/brainwashed by Fenrir in those two games, for example. And yet that's a thing in W5 now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T17:17:10-08:00","id":1530597,"title":"","content":"Just a tip, at this point it's already very difficult for either of you to convince the other of anything, let alone a sentence that in a week's time might not mean anything for reasons. So it's better to close before someone says something they shouldn't say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T18:43:25-08:00","id":1530599,"title":"","content":"I sent Jason Carl the question and am happy to concede the point unless he says otherwise. This is a good thread and I have no desire to belabor the issue.<br /> <br /> I'd rather discuss, &quot;Are the Garou STILL fighting the Wyrm or not?&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T20:10:22-08:00","id":1530608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1530599#post1530599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sent Jason Carl the question and am happy to concede the point unless he says otherwise. This is a good thread and I have no desire to belabor the issue.<br /> <br /> I'd rather discuss, &quot;Are the Garou STILL fighting the Wyrm or not?&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The answer to anything involving W5 is *shrugs apathetically and with excessive angst*.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T03:04:57-08:00","id":1530623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1530412#post1530412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That last one seems to be wrong based on info so far as we have 2 canon depictions of Cultists abandoning Caerns and one of them destroying a Caern.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is what happens when I talk about 5th Edition before quite finishing the core book \u2026<br /> <br /> On the other hand, given this IS a Cult, it\u2019s quite possible what they have \u2018on the books\u2019 isn\u2019t what they practice in the field (and if one assumes their version of the Litany is more or less PR, then I think it\u2019s still just about possible to salvage at least one little scrap of my pride). (-;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T03:13:37-08:00","id":1530625,"title":"","content":"For the record, my own attitude is that what\u2019s left of the Garou Nation is still fighting the Wyrm wherever opportunity allows: for my money the situation as described in the core book makes more sense as a slump from which Our Heroes (The PCs) have to rescue the Garou than as a final, irreversible decline.<br /> <br /> After all, if things were all rosy for Earth and her children, she wouldn\u2019t need Werewolf Spirit Warriors to hammer down villains and build up her defences in the first place (It also needs to be kept in mind that, while the Garou are a hammer and not every problem is a nail, a hammer is just as capable of building a house as it is of wrecking a house, given the right pair of hands).<br /> <br /> Others may have different opinions, but this is the one that gives me hope for wheresoever WEREWOLF goes from here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T03:13:51-08:00","id":1530626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1530599#post1530599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sent Jason Carl the question and am happy to concede the point unless he says otherwise. This is a good thread and I have no desire to belabor the issue.<br /> <br /> I'd rather discuss, &quot;Are the Garou STILL fighting the Wyrm or not?&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Look... this is just my guess, but I believe that where &quot;Fight the Wyrm&quot; intercedes with &quot;We need to survive&quot; they must fight, whether defending themselves or carrying out a preemptive attack and considering that there are even Garou using Wyrm resources she shouldn't be that villainous anymore, at least I imagine. Just to clarify, this would also imply that they fight against the Weaver and ultimately against the Wyld itself, but to answer the question, I think so.<br /> <br /> The reasons, they fought the Wyrm before and it would make sense for her to continue attacking them now, the Weaver would only eliminate obstacles, as for the Wyld, if they really aren't fighting for her anymore it wouldn't be strange for her to want to punish or encourage them them in some way and even if it wasn't the case, the spirits related to her could blame them for the apocalypse or something similar. This is of course me pulling information from old lore.<br /> <br /> If we include how vague W5 can be and in theory can be filled with anything, Garou may not even be related to the Triad and exist apart from it, in which case the Garou's condition could even be a disease or curse that always existed, or appeared during the apocalypse and the history of the Garou nation is a bedtime story and in fact it never really existed.<br /> <br /> Writing now I had a pretty crazy idea, what if the Garou have gone extinct before? Around the 17th or 18th century and without their presence, humanity grew and caused an imbalance and this imbalance messed with the spiritual world, bringing the Garou back? This would mix with the idea they introduced of blood memory of ancient people, it would make sense, these Garou with different thoughts about the Garou nation would come from there, they are memories of other ancients inserted into them and they are just putting the pieces together, but none of them have the whole memory, just parts. That's why everything is messed up. I'll try to elaborate on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T11:33:46-08:00","id":1530658,"title":"","content":"Personally I tend to run with the idea that while The Wyrm is still A Threat it\u2019s no longer THE Threat (Possibly because there\u2019s a \u2018Balance Wyrm\u2019 back in the mix somehow), since<br /> my feeling is that W5 makes a great deal more sense as a setting where The Weaver (A somewhat more morally-ambivalent threat) is in the ascendant.<br /> <br /> On the other hand I am fully prepared to 5th edition cockroach-spirits having an attitude towards local Glass Walkers which makes much, much more sense if one assumes that spirits can see past the Fourth Wall, and know when they\u2019ve been done Wrong, so take my suggestions with a pinch of salt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T07:24:48-08:00","id":1531880,"title":"","content":"I'm currently editing WHEN WILL YOU RAGE for re-release and it's interesting to note that the &quot;Get of Fenris are a bunch of pure monsters&quot; is something that apparently a lot of people had the view on throughout the game line. The portrayal of the Get here in this official product is gross and horrifying.<br /> <br /> Virtually every short story from this product has them doing something nightmarish awful with one story about the Swords of Heimdall and their involvement in the actual Nazi war crimes, another talking about how women are banished for trying to claim to be Ahrouns, and another still about their belief that the Impergium should be resumed against non-Garou kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Which is to say that the players may have flat out refused what was official canon to at least some developers for a long time.<br /> <br /> And you know what? That's fine because the official canon version was stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T07:36:40-08:00","id":1531883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1531880#post1531880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently editing WHEN WILL YOU RAGE for re-release and it's interesting to note that the &quot;Get of Fenris are a bunch of pure monsters&quot; is something that apparently a lot of people had the view on throughout the game line. The portrayal of the Get here in this official product is gross and horrifying.<br /> <br /> Virtually every short story from this product has them doing something nightmarish awful with one story about the Swords of Heimdall and their involvement in the actual Nazi war crimes, another talking about how women are banished for trying to claim to be Ahrouns, and another still about their belief that the Impergium should be resumed against non-Garou kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Which is to say that the players may have flat out refused what was official canon to at least some developers for a long time.<br /> <br /> And you know what? That's fine because the official canon version was stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't put any stock in those stories and the actual canon being the same. Even modern short stories for WtA leave out vast amounts of crucial mechanics for the sake of the story. The only ones that have been true to the game setting have been Song of Unmaking, the Silver Crown and the revised Tribe Novel series.<br /> <br /> When Will You Rage 1 and Drums Around the Fire are the oldest short story collections for WtA and it shows. Mind, Drums Around the Fire has some of my favourite stories for WtA, but they also take a lot of liberties for the sake of the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T08:51:11-08:00","id":1531888,"title":"","content":"I believe that the phrase that the developer used back in the day of the old forums was that the novels were &quot;canon on crack&quot;. That's why you got stories where there was a Garou who was also a Bastet, or the Crinos-born Garou knocking up an Imbued woman (double trouble, as Imbued can't have kids with the monsters!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T09:33:14-08:00","id":1531893,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Fiction is unreliable and When will You Rage is some of the oldest WtA Fiction there is.<br /> <br /> That said, - The Swords were absolute filth and thats why they were rooted out from their hidey hole and murderised.<br /> - some backwards Septs did have an attitude to female garou that they carried over from their human upbringing ( thats how/why the Valkyries established themselves, sure they could have gone over to the Furies but they were Fenrir and that meant standing their ground until the other guy moved...which by Revised they largely had.), but it was never the majority of the Tribe and it wasn't just a Fenrir thing....all sorts of stupid human attitudes got picked up by various Garou/Vampires/Mages etc.<br /> - There are small pockets of Garou who want to restart the Impergium all over the Nation including a bunch of Coggies, these Garou are colloquially known as idiots who don't think things through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T09:34:24-08:00","id":1531894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werew