used what was official canon to at least some developers for a long time.<br /> <br /> And you know what? That's fine because the official canon version was stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which canon? Because have a least 3 to this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T11:37:30-08:00","id":1531963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1531880#post1531880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently editing WHEN WILL YOU RAGE for re-release and it's interesting to note that the &quot;Get of Fenris are a bunch of pure monsters&quot; is something that apparently a lot of people had the view on throughout the game line. The portrayal of the Get here in this official product is gross and horrifying.<br /> <br /> Virtually every short story from this product has them doing something nightmarish awful with one story about the Swords of Heimdall and their involvement in the actual Nazi war crimes, another talking about how women are banished for trying to claim to be Ahrouns, and another still about their belief that the Impergium should be resumed against non-Garou kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Which is to say that the players may have flat out refused what was official canon to at least some developers for a long time.<br /> <br /> And you know what? That's fine because the official canon version was stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div> Given the very first GET OF FENRIS Tribebook starts with Sergeant Rage and his Howlin\u2019 Commandoes murdering Nazis (and also notes that, not only have She-wolves of the Fenrir been Jarls before, there\u2019s a whole durn camp of Werewolf Warrior Women) one suspects that not all authors writing the Get of Fenris have been reading from the same splatbook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T18:15:51-08:00","id":1531987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1530599#post1530599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather discuss, &quot;Are the Garou STILL fighting the Wyrm or not?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The short answer is, &quot;Of course.&quot; <br /> <br /> The Wyrm wants to destroy and corrupt the world, kill or twist every werewolf and everyone and everything thing that werewolf cares about. The only options are to fight the Wyrm, serve the Wyrm or die to the Wyrm. So even if a werewolf doesn't want to fight, they don't have much choice in the matter.<br /> <br /> The big change between the editions seems to be in how aggressive werewolves are in fighting the Wyrm. In earlier editions, the Litany commanding werewolves to fight the Wyrm wherever it breeds was very important. Werewolves would travel long distances (down to the Amazon or deep into the Umbra) to hunt down and fight the Wyrm. Things like Moonbridges made it fairl;y simple to travel vast distances without the ST or PC's getting bogged down in logistics. This also went back to the one of the basic concepts in environmentalism - that things which happen on the other side of the world can still have a direct effect on you.<br /> <br /> <br /> That seems less of the case in W5. The Tribes got together and decided they weren't going to go crusade and aggressively fight the Wyrm anymore. They were going to be more passive, and just defend their home bases, letting the Wyrm breed and grow stronger in its home bases. The Cult of Fenris is the group that's spending its time traveling around, fighting the Wyrm. So in W5, while werewolves absolutely do fight the Wyrm, it's generally only when the Wyrm shows up in that werewolf's neighborhood. Non-Cult werewolves typically aren't going to be going into the Wyrm's neighborhoods to kick ass. That's a big distinction between the presentation of the Cult of Fenris and the rest of the Werewolf Nation. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T18:27:28-08:00","id":1531988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528721-ten-tips-to-running-the-cult-of-fenris-in-werewolf-fifth-edition?p=1531987#post1531987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The short answer is, &quot;Of course.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1W7c8QghPxk\" target=\"_blank\">Once more with feeling!</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T06:42:07-08:00","id":1532016,"title":"","content":"You know, it just struck me that the list at the start of this thread was missing one point and therefore ought to be ELEVEN Tips.<br /> <br /> The first point of this version would, of course, be STAY ANGRY.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T14:22:04-08:00","id":1532112,"title":"","content":"Alright, I probably deserved that thumb\u2019s down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-08T13:47:45-08:00","id":1532255,"title":"","content":"It reminds me some Glass Walkers quote - you have to include Fenris in your plans cause the tribe is so stupid that they will do Something unexpected- something like that.<br /> <br /> I was trying to solve the Cult puzzle and to fit them in my game so the first idea is that they are not the bad guys. Second and later:<br /> - their goal is the same as others but methods are different<br /> - cult is still Get and they are doing what Get have been doing all the time: destroying Wyrm, invading caerns and ,,secure&quot; them, only strong survive<br /> - they are always unpredictable<br /> - they are bloody handed heroes even if other don't look at them this wsy<br /> - Cult may be the only way to reconstruct Garou Nation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T05:03:01-07:00","id":1532366,"title":"","content":"Hngh. Well that\u2019s one way to do it, though if you\u2019re going to show 